\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Fall of the Chilean peso reflects the difficulty of the battle against the strength of the dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  received a boost in mid-July with a US$25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but has recently had one of the worst performances in the region in an example of how difficult the battle to counter a rampant dollar is, according to a Reuters analysis.\par \par \uc2 It is now threatening to break the 1,000 pesos per dollar barrier again after reaching a historic low of close to 1,050 pesos in July, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched its plan of spot sales of dollars for up to 10 billion dollars and exchange hedging instruments for the same amount.\par \par \uc2 In addition, it offered a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap plan for up to US$5 billion. The move successfully helped to eliminate peso volatility.\par \par \uc2 However, as the dollar soars and interest rate hikes by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  impact global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the British pound to the Japanese yen and Chinese yuan, the effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  fades.\par \par \uc2 In the past two months, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened 6.5% against the dollar, trailing the region's major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil, Mexico, Peru and Colombia. And it could weaken further after Friday's end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, as set.\par \par \uc2 "Probably in the short term, maybe in October, we will see 1,000 pesos (per dollar) and maybe it will extend historical maximum that we have," said Angel Rubilar, senior analyst at Santiago-based Libertex. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now worth 968 units to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chile is not alone in having to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have increased in India, the Philippines and Korea in recent weeks, while Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has just spent a record 2.8 billion yen (US$19.7 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the yen fell to a 24-year low of nearly 146 per dollar, triggered a sharp rebound of more than 5 yen per dollar, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell back to around 144.7.\par \par \uc2 Diego Mora, market strategist at XTB Latam, said the \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped reduce the chances of aggressive moves, but the measure has its limits.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful for the objective sought by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was to control exchange rate volatility but not the price," he said, adding that markets had already incorporated the end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We have seen a reduction in volatility. The possibility of seeing aggressive rises is less," he added.\par \par \uc2 Chile, the world's largest copper and second-largest lithium producer, is also grappling with annual inflation of around 14% through August, weak red metal prices and a recession expected by 2023, compounding the impact of the strong dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Juan Prada of \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said tightening global financial conditions were increasing pressure on some regional markets particularly susceptible to external global economic shocks.\par \par \uc2 "We have identified Chile and Colombia as vulnerable, and the COP (Colombian peso) and CLP (Chilean peso) have underperformed their Latin American peers" since the September meeting of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee.\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given no indication of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts and traders say that, despite the pressures, another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be "hasty" and could jeopardize long-term stability by affecting reserve levels.\par \par \uc2 "Reserves are not infinite," Mora referred. "To the extent that a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has less direct foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the country becomes riskier with its long-term rates," he said.\par \par \uc2 With information from Reuters\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221004eia400a9p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
