\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Chile's sliding peso reflects tough battle vs rampaging dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2022\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Oct 3 (Reuters) - Chile's sliding peso got a shot in the arm in July from a huge $25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but in recent months has been one of the region's worst performers, showing how hard the battle is for policy makers countering a rampaging dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is threatening to breach the 1,000 peso per dollar line once again after it hit a record low near 1,050 pesos in July. That milestone led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to launch a plan to sell $20 billion in dollars and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments, backed up by a $5 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap and peso liquidity program.\par \par \uc2 That move successfully helped cull wild volatility.\par \par \uc2 However, as the U.S. dollar soars and interest rate hikes by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  hammer global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the British sterling to the Japanese yen and Chinese yuan, the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has faded.\par \par \uc2 In the last two months the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened some 6.5% versus the dollar, trailing major regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil, Mexico, Peru and Colombia. It is likely to weaken more after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program on Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 "Probably in the short term, maybe in October we'll see 1,000 pesos (to the dollar) and maybe we'll beat our historic low," said Angel Rubilar, a Santiago-based senior analyst at Libertex. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now worth 968 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chile is not alone in having to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have increased in India, the Philippines and Korea in recent weeks, while Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 2.8 trillion yen ($19.7 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week.\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following the yen's slump to a 24-year low of nearly 146 to the dollar, triggered a sharp bounce of more than 5 yen per dollar, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drifted down again to around 144.7.\par \par \uc2 'RESERVES AREN'T INFINITE'\par \par \uc2 Diego Mora, a market strategist for XTB Latam, said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped reduce the chances of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, but had its limits.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful for what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed, which was controlling volatility in the exchange rate, but not the price," said Mora, noting that markets were already pricing in the end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week.\par \par \uc2 "The possibility of a sharp crash is lower."\par \par \uc2 Chile, the world's top producer of copper and the No. 2 for electric vehicle battery metal lithium, is also grappling with annual inflation at some 14%, weakening copper prices and a predicted recession, compounding the hit from the strong dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Juan Prada at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said the tightening of global financial conditions was ramping up pressure on some regional markets particularly susceptible to external global economic impacts.\par \par \uc2 "We have identified Chile and Colombia as vulnerable, and COP (Colombian peso) and CLP (Chilean peso) have underperformed LatAm peers" since the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting in September, he said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, has given no indication that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. Analysts and traders say that despite pressures, another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be "hasty" and could risk longer-term stability by denting levels of reserves.\par \par \uc2 "Reserves aren't infinite," Mora added. "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has less direct reserves of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country becomes riskier with its long-term interest rates."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alexander Villegas and Natalia Ramos; Additional reporting by Karin Strohecker in London; Editing by Adam Jourdan and Richard Chang) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-3T12:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221003eia301ta3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
