85B0721100016F800C0FA003C0A0003AC00D76700D70800057F005C0C004D81180035AE0015A900A77500C86E12C301110003B}}
\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar approaches $1,000 again due to global uncertainty and analysts believe that the CB should not think about a new  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  yet.\b0\par\par\uc2 1,175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 At a time when the end of the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is approaching, the dollar once again appears on the horizon as a threat. Already rising steadily in the last week and a half, this Monday it lashed out strongly and closed with a rise of more than $20, reaching $992. This is its highest level since July 15 ($975), just the day after the exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed to its historical maximum of $1,051.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the dollar recorded its eighth consecutive day of increase, if the two holidays on working days that took place during the Fiestas Patrias are discounted, accumulating a gain of $93.61 since September 12.\par \par \uc2 But this situation is not just Chile's. The Chilean peso is losing strength amid fears of a global recession that is pushing commodity prices into a slump. World markets are internalizing a new scenario where the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  would raise its interest rate harder and longer in order to control inflation. This leads investors to avoid risky assets, highlighted \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 . Along with the Chilean peso, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply against the dollar on the day, with the euro and the pound sterling, for example, at historic levels.\par \par \uc2 Also on Monday morning, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advisor, Stephany Griffith-Jones, said that the issuing institution "is closely monitoring" the dollar's movements, while participating in an activity organized by the Universidad de O'Higgins.\par \par \uc2 This scenario comes only four days before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ends its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. And although during the morning there was speculation as to what the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would do given this new situation, this question ended in the afternoon, as it issued a communiqu\u233\'00\'E9 reaffirming the end of this process.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  informs that, as foreseen in the announcement dated July 14, 2022, the program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive provision of liquidity in dollars will end on Friday, September 30, 2022. Therefore, as of October 2, 2022, spot dollar sales, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap and Repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cease", said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of the aforementioned date, the CB informed that "only the renewal of the stock of forward dollar sales \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be offered, at market conditions, of the stock in force as of today, for the equivalent of US$ 9,110 million. If any auction is declared void, this amount will be rescheduled for the following week".\par \par \uc2 This renewal scheme will be in effect until Friday, January 13, 2023. Eventual changes to this renewal mechanism, as a result of changes in market conditions, will be announced in due course, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's evaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is positive: "The Council of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  considers that the program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive provision of liquidity in dollars has achieved the objective of helping the proper functioning of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, facilitating the adjustment of the economy and the financial markets to external and internal conditions".\par \par \uc2 For this reason, the Board maintains its commitment to the floating exchange rate regime, and reserves "the option to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market in exceptional circumstances if it considers that the proper functioning of the financial market is at risk", it added.\par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's information, of the total amount destined to the sale of spot dollars, as of today a total of US$ 5,950 million has been allotted and that by the end of Friday this amount will reach US$ 6,100 million out of a total of US$ 10,000 million.\par \par \uc2 With this process, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves went from US$45 billion to US$39 billion.\par \par \uc2 Experts agree that this is not the time for the CB to go out again with an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, since the causes are global and the appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with the fundamentals, so there are no signs of a misalignment. "Behind the most recent rise we recognize mainly external factors. The price of copper has retreated and the global dollar has gained value, reaching record highs, given the prospect of more aggressive Fed rate hikes," comments Bci's chief economist, Sergio Lehmann. However, he states that "we see that risk premiums on Chilean assets remain very high. Uncertainty, although it reveals better defined edges today, is still high". This, for Lehmann, is mainly due to political factors. "Important discrepancies are recognized within the government coalition on key issues, such as pension reform, trade agreements, figures related to Chile's development in recent years and others, which introduce volatility".\par \par \uc2 Tom\u225\'00\'E1s Flores, economist at Libertad y Desarrollo (LyD), adds that "this new rise of the dollar in Chile is being repeated in several countries as a consequence of the present and future rise of interest rates in the US. At the same time, the cut in growth projections for the world is affecting the prices of commodities, including copper, which additionally affects our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Another view is provided by economist Patricio Rojas, of Rojas y Asociados, who argues that "as the expectation is that the United States will raise interest rates more strongly and the possibility of a deeper deceleration and even recession in some parts of the world, the dollar will of course gain ground. This is the origin of the peso's depreciation".\par \par \uc2 What the authorities should doFor now, economists point out in that the CB has to wait. "A dollar at $990 we all agree is not a sustainable value over time. Clearly the timing of the end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not the best given the global context. And therefore, thinking about some kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be within its powers," says Rojas.\par \par \uc2 Martina Ogaz, an economist at Euroamerica, adds that "for the moment, I believe that the conditions have not been met to extend \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the current depreciation of the parity has been in line with the fundamentals and has not registered anomalous volatility or spread to other local markets.\par \par \uc2 Juan Ortiz, senior economist at OCEC-UDP, shares the same view: "I believe that the conditions are not yet in place. The peso has depreciated sharply as a result mainly of the strengthening of the multilateral dollar. The CB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it considers that, due to exchange rate fundamentals, the exchange rate is misaligned, which is not the case today, as can be seen from the behavior of the peso with respect to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Lehmann points out that "the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will monitor the evolution of the exchange market with special care. Today the exchange rate misalignment is high, around 10% according to our models, and volatility is extraordinarily high. If this worsens and affects the functioning of the financial market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we do not see that for now".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220927ei9r00b1v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
