\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar starts sixth day on the rise and surpasses $950 two weeks before the plebiscite\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The intense bullish pressures of last week are once again imposing themselves on the dollar, pushing it above the $ 950 mark in a local and international investment environment that favors the appreciation of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 , the dollar is up $ 9.60 to trade at $ 954.20 at 9 am.\par \par \uc2 Last week was the week of the greatest advance for the exchange rate in all its history of free floating, with an increase of $ 67.60 in the set of five upward days (transactions on holiday Monday were minimal, which did not prevent a rise in the price).\par \par \uc2 "The dollar continues on its upward path on the eve of the exit plebiscite next Sunday, September 4 in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we could see the exchange rate above $1,000 again in the days leading up to the referendum," said \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Globe market analyst Sergio Cisternas.\par \par \uc2 In addition, copper fell 0.12% to US$ 3.64 per pound on the \uc2 London Metal Exchange\uc2 , contributing to the weakening of the Chilean peso.\par \par \uc2 Global dollar The rise of the dollar is also due to international factors linked to a decrease in investors' confidence regarding future financial conditions, as it is expected that the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  will not hesitate to raise interest rates sharply.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index - which measures the global strength of the dollar - traded higher for the fourth consecutive day, rising 0.20% to 108.38 points.\par \par \uc2 "The next key event to gauge U.S. dollar risk will be this Friday's speech by Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  at the Jackson Hole symposium," wrote analysts at \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The anticipation of such an event, in the absence of an August policy meeting, has led all types of riskier assets to experience pullbacks.\par \par \uc2 According to Oanda senior analyst \uc2 Craig Erlam\uc2 , "traders will be looking for more clarity when Powell speaks, and seem to think his appearance will take the form of a dovish warning".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220822ei8m005t7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
