\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's volatile peso extends rally after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2022\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, July 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has enjoyed an extended rally since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week announced a $25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buoy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a series of historic lows, but it may face a bumpier path in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 At Tuesday's close, the peso finished up 1.81% at 923.80 per dollar, taking its gains to 13.21% from a historic low of 1,045.80 on Thursday, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the peso was aided by a hike in the price of copper, of which Chile is the world's largest producer, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its strong run on Tuesday even as the price of the metal fell.\par \par \uc2 "For a lot of people the question is why the (exchange rate) keeps (improving) after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fall of copper today," said Jorge Selaive, chief economist of \uc2 Scotiabank Chile\uc2 , adding that other internal factors are aiding the peso's ascent.\par \par \uc2 Selaive said a "brutal" drop in risk fund shares in the country's AFP pension system is leading to investment in more conservative funds, resulting in AFPs selling dollars, aiding the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 As well, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't announced how it will "sterilize" the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or remove the excess dollars it is injecting into the system through daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions, but signs point to the bank letting bonds with less than a 360-day maturity expire.\par \par \uc2 Many of those bonds were issued at lower rates before a recent string of rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 "So the effect of the lowered interest rate will concentrate in that time frame," he said.\par \par \uc2 Another contributing factor is that foreign investors are holding off on buying dollar futures contracts, he said.\par \par \uc2 "They're waiting for the exchange rate to stabilize at new levels to reevaluate their strategy in Chile," Selaive said.\par \par \uc2 A global surge in the U.S. dollar has pushed down \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worldwide, but Chile's peso has been particularly volatile, partly due to its floating exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 That has made it more susceptible to speculation related to copper's fluctuating price and political uncertainty over a proposed new constitution, as well as the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Victor Salas and other economists at the University of Santiago.\par \par \uc2 "This is going to be an unclear, unclean drop in the exchange rate," in terms of the number of pesos that a U.S. dollar can buy, Salas said, adding that the real effect will take weeks to see.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Fabian Cambero and Alexander Villegas; editing by Richard Pullin)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-23T11:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220720ei7k01sl1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
