\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  tells U.S. investors about  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention \highlight\uc2  and tax plans\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 New York, 18 Jul. The Chilean government explained to US investors on Monday its latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the tax reform plans of President \uc2 Gabriel Boric\uc2 , with the message that it continues to be "an open economy".\par \par \uc2 The "Chile Day" event organized by InBest and which had been planned as an occasion to "position Chile as a leading exporter of financial services in Latin America" was rather an exposition of the need for these economic policies of a government that a priori can be seen as less friendly to capital due to its leftist ideology.\par \par \uc2 The governor of the \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Rosanna Costa, and the Minister of Finance, \uc2 Mario Marcel\uc2 , spoke, explaining the expansive policies that Chile had to apply to get out of the pandemic crisis and how it has now had to apply adjustments in the face of a very high accumulated inflation (12.5% in the last 12 months) and a dollar at historic highs that exceeded the 1,000 peso barrier.\par \par \uc2 Costa emphasized that the country, although it has suffered an unprecedented shock in recent years, enjoys "a solid institutional framework" that will allow it to face the high public debt and, even more of a priority because it is now "the main concern", to aim at lowering inflation to 3% within two years, he stressed.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Marcel -an economist well regarded in the business world- acknowledged that his country is facing an unprecedented accumulation of problems: high raw material prices, rising private consumption, a historically expensive dollar and supply bottlenecks, which have forced his government to adopt restrictive monetary policies.\par \par \uc2 He took for granted that the recession will arrive this year, but he expressed hope that in early 2023 there will be a recovery, thanks to last Thursday's "successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the exchange market, which in a few days allowed the exchange rate to drop below the psychological barrier of 1,000 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Marcel dedicated the last part of his speech to defend the fiscal reform planned by the Government to revert a fiscal distribution "currently seen as unfair" and also to correct the fact that the tax burden is now much lower than in other countries of the \uc2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\uc2  (\uc2 OECD\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220719ei7j00508\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
