\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar opens below 1,000 pesos after  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Santiago de \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 18. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  this Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday, with an injection of 25 billion dollars to the market to contain a historic escalation above 1,000 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Although it is still at high levels, at the beginning of trading the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  averaged 945 pesos, a fall of almost 3% and more than 100 pesos in two days, according to the Chilean Electronic Stock Exchange.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the rise in the price of copper played in favor of the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with futures fixed at 2.78 % at 3.32 dollars per pound of the red metal, the main export of the South American country.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be through the sale of spot dollars for an amount of up to 10 billion dollars, the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments for an amount of up to 10 billion dollars and a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program for an amount of up to 5 billion dollars from July 18 to September 30, 2022.\par \par \uc2 This move, expected by the markets, came on the same day that the dollar reached its all-time high of 1,051 pesos per unit and one day after the issuer raised benchmark interest rates by 75 points to 9.75% to try to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean economy grew by a historic 11.7% in 2021, after a sharp 5.8% drop in 2020 due to the pandemic, and recorded cumulative inflation of 7.2%, the highest in 14 years.\par \par \uc2 In May, the government lowered its growth forecast for 2022 from 3.5% to 1.5% and raised its 12-month cumulative inflation estimate for the end of the year to 8.9%.\par \par \uc2 The issuer did not make an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of such magnitude since March 2020 November 2019 (20 billion dollars), when the peso reached 828.36 units per dollar and the country was plunged into the biggest social crisis in its recent history, with protests that left at least thirty dead. EFE\par \par \uc2 ssb/mmm/eat\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220718ei7i0069t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
