\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar maintains its free fall after  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention \highlight\uc2  and copper price hike\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues its downward trend, which started after the announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar market. In addition, the rise in the price of copper and the weakening of the greenback at international level give another hand to the Chilean peso.\par \par \uc2 At the beginning of trading, the dollar fell $33.72 after Friday's close and traded at a value of $944.78 . Thus, in two days, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost more than $100 and continues to move away from the $1,000 barrier.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, copper helps the Chilean peso after registering a rise in its three-month price. Copper futures are up 2.78% to a value of US$3.32 per pound.\par \par \uc2 Prices of copper and other industrial metals rebounded on Monday as investors bought back positions on news of government support for the economy in China, the main metals consumer, and a weaker dollar, Reuters noted.\par \par \uc2 "This is still a bear market rebound, and it is too early to predict whether this will turn into a consolidation and a recovery," \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2 's head of commodity strategy in Copenhagen, \uc2 Ole Hansen\uc2 , told the news agency.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the international dollar weakened again after falling on Friday on expectations that the next rate hike by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed) will not be 100 basis points and will be moderated to 75 basis points. The new forecasts are based on recent statements from Fed members.\par \par \uc2 Along these lines, the dollar index is down 0.47% from the previous close and is moving away from its 20-year high.\par \par \uc2 "It is possible that we may see some additional correction of the dollar in our country, to return in the coming days with possible rises considering the more fundamental fundamentals of the exchange rate", commented the head of trading studies at Capitaria, Ricardo Bustamante.\par \par \uc2 However, the senior market analyst of XTB Latam, Juan Ortiz Godoy, states that "the factors that are appreciating the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still latent, so we could see higher levels in the exchange rate as the days go by while the fears of an economic recession continue to persist and copper continues to fall".\par \par \uc2 So far today, the Chilean peso is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has appreciated the most against the dollar in the world, according to Bloomberg.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220718ei7i005q5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
