\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention \highlight\uc2  in the dollar market should help bonds in  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar spot market announced Thursday night triggered the largest daily rally in the peso in four decades and lowered swap rates and bond yields. Its impact will reverberate through the market for weeks.\par \par \uc2 The bank plans to sell US$10 billion in the spot market by September 30, plus a similar amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges and US$5 billion in swaps. The peso appreciated as much as 9.9% on Friday following the announcement.\par \par \uc2 How the dollar market works: Banks, brokers and more than US$1.2 billion traded per dayThe peso's new strength should help restore the local bond market.\par \par \uc2 "We expect greater liquidity in fixed income markets and a consequent fall in long-term yields," analysts at Larrain Vial, including head of research, Leonardo Suarez, wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 The rebound in the peso eased the outlook for import costs and inflation, prompting a 22 basis point drop in two-year swap rates on Friday from an all-time high of 10.05%. The yield on Chilean Treasury bonds maturing in 2026 fell 35 basis points on the same day, while one-year break-even inflation plunged to 9.5% from an all-time high of 10.2%.\par \par \uc2 "The fall in the exchange rate should imply a moderation of inflation expectations, this should benefit nominal rates over UF rates," said Marco Gallardo, deputy fixed income manager at BICE Inversiones. However, in the short term he still prefers to bet on short UF bonds, considering that inflation will be higher in the coming months as the peso recovers, he said.\par \par \uc2 Falling from highsThere are still structural factors that will slow the adjustment in fixed income, said Sergio Lehmann, chief economist at BCI. Bond recovery "will be happening anyway, but without reaching the values of a few years ago," he commented. "In that sense there is already damage in our markets."\par \par \uc2 Crisis, what crisis?It was a bold move on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given that they only have US$45.8 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which represents about 5.2 months of imports. They had little choice, however, after the Finance Ministry's announcement that it planned to sell US$5 billion had almost no impact on the market a few weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 "This is probably one of the most successful \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its history of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Jorge Selaive, chief economist at \uc2 Scotiabank \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in a tweet on Friday. The program just goes into effect today.\par \par \uc2 The plan is big enough to have an impact, but it will probably take several sessions for the market to fully absorb its impact, said Nathan Pincheira, chief economist at Fynsa, who forecast the peso could reach 920 pesos to the U.S. dollar in the coming weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 974 pesos to the dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso had depreciated 21% since the beginning of June. Alvaro Vivanco, director of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 NatWest Markets\uc2 , described the situation as a "full-blown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis". It remains the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world during that period, even after Friday's rally.\par \par \uc2 Confidence in the peso had fallen so low that it even gave up 4% on Thursday, the day after monetary policymakers raised the key interest rate by 75 basis points to 9.75%.\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Rosanna Costa said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market retained adequate liquidity, but that the board was concerned about the "cumulative effect" of peso volatility on other markets. She also emphasized that the measures were aimed at "making the peso more stable" and not directly at the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Continued in Pulse Euro hits one-week highs: retreat in Fed rate hike bets hits dollarImmigrants now account for almost 11% of AFP affiliates: five years ago they were only 3%.Consumer confidence falls in June to its lowest level since October 2021 due to higher inflationLabor Minister for the 40-hour project: "We are convinced that it will be good for Chilean society".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220718ei7i004zx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
