\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was highly expected by the market, given the significant increase in volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is appropriate because the market had been depreciating in addition to what the fundamentals indicated.\par \par \uc2 Martina Ogaz, analyst at Euroamerica\par \par \uc2 The Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  announced that, in order to facilitate the Chilean economy's adjustment to uncertain and changing domestic and external conditions, it decided to implement a program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive liquidity provision in dollars, for up to US$25 billion, starting next Monday, July 18, through September 30, 2022.\par \par \uc2 Through a statement published on Thursday night on the entity's official website, it pointed out that the external determinants of the exchange rate in Chile have continued to deteriorate "significantly. In particular, since the beginning of June the global dollar has appreciated about 7% and the price of copper has fallen approximately 30 percent. In a context of local uncertainty that remains high, this has continued to put downward pressure on the Chilean peso".\par \par \uc2 In recent days, however, they acknowledged that "the peso depreciation has occurred with unusually high intensity and volatility, which has strained the price formation of the exchange market. The persistence of this scenario increases the likelihood of significant distortions in the functioning of the financial market in general".\par \par \uc2 In particular, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market considers: the sale of spot dollars for an amount of up to 10 billion dollars and the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments for an amount of up to 10 billion dollars.\par \par \uc2 The monetary effects in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be duly sterilized, explained the bank, "so that the provision of liquidity in pesos is consistent with the monetary policy rate".\par \par \uc2 Regarding the provision of dollar liquidity, although the dollar money market is functioning adequately, the Board considered it appropriate to offer a "preemptive" \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program for up to 5 billion dollars. This will be complemented by a peso liquidity program through over-the-counter REPO \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same maturities.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will inform at the end of each week the amount and other terms and conditions of the following week's auctions. It will also publish timely information about the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out, indicating in aggregate form the amounts of these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Board reiterated that it will continue to use all the tools at its disposal to maintain the normal functioning of domestic and external payments, and that inflation will remain within the 3% target over the two-year policy horizon.\par \par \uc2 For her part, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest authority, Rosanna Costa, admitted that "it was a complicated decision. Our objective is for the exchange rate to be at a level more consistent with its fundamentals".\par \par \uc2 Following the announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar recorded a sharp decline on Friday, after a successive wave of record highs that took the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above $1,050 in Thursday's session. At Friday's opening, the dollar traded at $997.00, down $54 from Thursday's close, then moved to $1,000 levels before dropping again and deepening its retreat to close at $978.50, down $72.5.\par \par \uc2 Samuel Carrasco, senior economist at Credicorp Capital, commented on the announcement: "We value positively the magnitude of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, which in turn, should be complemented with a somewhat hawkish monetary policy path and reinforcing the message that rates will remain high for most of 2023".\par \par \uc2 For his part, Sergio Lehmann, chief economist at BCI, considered that "there were sufficient arguments for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220718ei7i001d4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
