\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Who are the favorites to replace \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  in the United Kingdom?\b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The former Minister of Finance \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  and the Deputy Minister of International Trade \uc2 Penny Mordaunt\uc2 , obtained enough support to pass to the second round of votes to elect the successor of the British Prime Minister, \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , reported the television channel 'Sky News'.\par \par \uc2 According to this media, Sunak has the support of no less than 50 party colleagues and Mordaunt, at least 30. To advance to the second round a candidate must have the support of at least 30 members of the Conservative Party. Among the candidates who made it through to the second round on July 13 were: former Finance Minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 ; Foreign Secretary \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 ; Finance Minister \uc2 Nadhim Zahawi\uc2 ; former Foreign Secretary \uc2 Jeremy Hunt\uc2 ; Deputy International Trade Minister \uc2 Penny Mordaunt\uc2 ; House of Commons committee chairman \uc2 Tom Tugendhat\uc2 ; Attorney General for England and Wales \uc2 Suella Braverman\uc2 ; former Equalities Minister \uc2 Kemi Badenoch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Later in the day, \uc2 Graham Brady\uc2 , chairman of the 1922 Committee, or the Conservative Private Members' Committee, announced that six candidates for the position of U.K. prime minister advanced to the second round of voting. The second round of voting will be held on July 14.\par \par \uc2 A total of 11 MPs declared their desire to run for Conservative leader and British prime minister, but three of them - Transport Minister \uc2 Grant Shapps\uc2 , former Health Minister \uc2 Sajid Javid\uc2  and former Conservative Party deputy prime minister \uc2 Rehman Chishti\uc2  - withdrew from the race. A candidate must have the support of at least 30 party members to advance to the second round, and more may be held until only two contenders remain. The winner will then be elected by the entire Conservative Party membership, which currently numbers about 200,000, with voting to be conducted by postal ballot. \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , in office as Prime Minister since July 2019, announced his resignation following a flurry of resignations from his ministers and senior officials.\par \par \uc2 An unprecedented crisis in the \uc2 British government\uc2  broke out after a sex scandal with MP Christopher Pincher, a Johnson supporter, accused of harassing two visitors to a London club. Johnson, who will remain in office until a new Chief of Staff is appointed, leaves the United Kingdom mired in a deep economic crisis and with the highest inflation recorded since 1982.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive liquidity provision in the amount of 25 billion dollars, to curb the historic rise of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Council of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile, in order to facilitate the adjustment of the Chilean economy to the uncertain and changing internal and external conditions, has decided to implement a program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive provision of liquidity in dollars, for an amount of up to 25 billion dollars starting next Monday [July 18] and until September 30, 2022," the agency stated in a press release.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  detailed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market contemplates the sale of spot dollars for an amount of up to 10 billion dollars, in addition to the sale of exchange hedging instruments for a similar amount.\par \par \uc2 "Since the beginning of June, the dollar at a global level has appreciated close to 7% and the price of copper [Chile's main export product] has fallen approximately 30%, this, in a context of local uncertainty that remains high, pressures the Chilean peso downwards", explained the issuing agency.\par \par \uc2 This month in Chile the dollar surpassed for the first time in history the barrier of 1,000 Chilean pesos, and this July 14 closed at 1,051 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220717ei7h002y0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
