\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  announcements lower the dollar in  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  and increase the purchasing power of travelers\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar reacted downward on Friday in Chile after the announcement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of an exchange and liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of up to 25 billion dollars to facilitate the adjustment of the economy in view of the uncertain internal and external conditions that have taken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to historic prices in the South American country.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as much as 50 pesos at the beginning of the day's trading, almost the same 51 pesos it rose on Thursday, when it reached 1,062 pesos, making it the largest increase since 1999. After midday it averaged 992 pesos.\par \par \uc2 The market reacted to the announcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which on Thursday night stated that "in order to facilitate the adjustment of the Chilean economy to the uncertain and changing internal and external conditions'', it will begin on Monday, July 18, a program of exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive provision of liquidity for up to 25,000 million dollars. The measure will be extended until September 30.\par \par \uc2 Simultaneously, the Chilean peso strengthened after a depreciation that "has occurred with an unusually high intensity and volatility", which since the beginning of the year has been around 20%, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred despite a new fall in the value of copper, Chile's main export, which has contracted by around 30% since the beginning of June.\par \par \uc2 Chile imports all the oil it consumes, as well as natural gas and diesel, and almost 2/3 of the products that make up the basket used to calculate inflation are imported.\par \par \uc2 The advance in the price of the dollar occurs in a context of global strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the strong fall of copper, which is also hit by the drop in the growth of China, the main buyer of the Chilean red metal.\par \par \uc2 The autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  described the measures adopted by its Board as exceptional and said that they are in line with its monetary policy, which responds to an inflationary target and exchange rate flexibility.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Mario Marcel\uc2  said that "we believe that it has been appropriate that it has used its powers for this purpose''.\par \par \uc2 Chile's 12-month inflation is 12.5%, and so far this year stands at 7.1%, more than double the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3%, which it expects to recover in about two years, after further adjustments to its interest rate, which it raised from 9% to 9.75% on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220717ei7g0008q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
