\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Chile central bank \highlight\uc2  announces $25 billion  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  amid U.S. dollar advance\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par 20:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Corrects sales program calendar to reflect end date of September 30, not July 30)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, July 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to a $25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market due to the galloping advance of the U.S. dollar in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released Thursday night, the bank said the peso has depreciated with unusually high intensity and volatility over the last few days, putting pressure on the prices of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The persistence of this scenario raises the probability that significant distortions will be generated in the functioning of the financial market in general," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 The announcement boosted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which gained 4.73% on Friday morning, dropping below 1,000 units per dollar. The previous day it closed with a drop of 3.7% to the minimum historical 1,045.80/1,046.10 units per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the U.S. dollar's strong global advance since June, the drop in the price of copper, Chile's main export, and "local uncertainty."\par \par \uc2 "This is a welcome development, particularly if combined with a decisive conventional monetary policy strategy," Alberto Ramos, an economist at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , said in a report.\par \par \uc2 "However, there are limits to what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can achieve given the very challenging domestic and external context and when taking into account the limited amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves."\par \par \uc2 The bank announced a $10 billion sales program on the spot market from July 18 to September 30 and the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments for the same amount.\par \par \uc2 "The monetary effects in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be duly sterilized, so that the provision of liquidity in pesos is consistent with the monetary policy rate," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, to increase the provision of liquidity in dollars, it will offer a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap plan for up to $5 billion, complemented by a liquidity program in pesos.\par \par \uc2 "These exceptional measures are consistent with the monetary policy scheme, based on an inflation target and exchange rate flexibility," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the week, the bank had said that the current deterioration of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not significantly affected the financial system, although it said it would continue to assess the situation in order to act if necessary.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Chilean peso closed down 3.7% at a record low of 1,045.80/1,046.10 per dollar. (Report by Fabi\u225\'00\'E1n Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Cambero; Writing by Alexander Villegas; Editing by Raissa Kasolowsky and Jonathan Oatis)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-18T18:34:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220715ei7f02tjl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
