\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile intervenes \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate with US$ 25 billion to defend the peso\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced plans to support the peso after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted to a record low, fueling inflation that is already at nearly four times the target.\par \par \uc2 Thursday night, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will carry out a $25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between July 18 and September 30. The plan includes up to $10 billion in spot market dollar sales and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging that could amount to the same amount.\par \par \uc2 "With the global recession narrative beginning to dominate the investment landscape, the \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to stop the downward momentum in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Todd Schubert, head of fixed income research at \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2 . The fall in copper prices has led to a sharp depreciation of the peso, as Chile is the world's largest copper producer, he said.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso fell to a record low of 1,060.40 per dollar on Thursday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened globally and copper prices plunged. The peso has already depreciated nearly 19 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 The announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after Finance Minister \uc2 Mario Marcel\uc2  said the government was studying ways to alleviate the effects of the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to comment on the matter.\par \par \uc2 Monetary policy makers have already extended aggressive interest rate hikes in an effort to tame annual inflation that probably rose to 12.7 percent in June, according to estimates in a Bloomberg survey. A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes imported goods more expensive, adding to price pressures.\par \par \uc2 Political uncertainty is also hurting the peso. Chile is approaching a referendum on Sept. 4 on a proposed new constitution. Polls show that more voters are inclined to reject the draft document, while a bill to reduce the majority needed to reform the current charter is making its way through congress.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented exchange rate measures in 2019, when the peso collapsed amid mass street protests, and again in 2020, at the start of the pandemic. The policies included dollar sales and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps.\par \par \uc2 Russia wants to create its own benchmark price for oil\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220717ei7f000ff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
