\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains as dollar eases;  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's peso outperforms on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par 21:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announces $25 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     * Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  modifies rate strategy\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew and Devik Jain\par     July 15 (Reuters) - Chile's peso shot up as much as 9.8% on\par Friday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from\par record lows, while a pause in the dollar prompted gains in most\par other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on track for its best\par session ever as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  agreed to a $25 billion\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to a rallying dollar, the drop in the price of\par copper, Chile's main export, and "local uncertainty."\par \par     Bets about an aggressive move by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par this month and safe-haven appeal amid recession worries have\par powered the dollar to near two-decade highs.\par     The peso breached 1,060 per dollar for the first time on\par Thursday and has been in record low territory for over three\par weeks. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  move lifted it to 974.2 on Friday.\par     "$25 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a country like \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  where GDP\par is not very big is remarkable. There is no doubt that this is\par going to be an outperformer in the aftermath of the program,"\par said Marcos Casarin, chief LatAm economist at Oxford Economics\par in Mexico.\par     "We found the Chilean peso over 20% undervalued before this\par announcement, so the discount is too big. We understand their\par political risks revolving around the new constitution, but at\par the same time the fundamentals don't look so bad."\par     Mexico's peso rose 1.26% as the dollar took a\par breather as two of the Fed's most hawkish policymakers said\par overnight they favored another 75-basis-point hike after hot\par U.S. inflation had raised bets of a 100 bps move this month. \par     As oil prices recovered, crude exporter Colombia's peso\par  firmed 3.06% to 4349.6, further recovering from the\par record low of 4,658.02 hit earlier this week. Colombia's retail\par sales rose 34.8% in May from a year earlier.\par     Brazil's real gained 0.5% in volatile trading.\par     Stocks in the region rose 1.9%, tracking\par Wall Street after upbeat U.S. retail sales data allayed concerns\par about an imminent recession.\par     However, Argentina's heavily controlled peso fell\par 0.16%. A \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bloomberg\f28 \uc2 \f2  report said Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its\par benchmark interest rate at 52%, according to a person with\par direct knowledge of the matter, as inflation galloped to 64% in\par the 12 months to June.\par     Meanwhile, Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday announced a\par change in its strategy for setting the country's interest rates,\par seeking to achieve positive real interest rates, which is part\par of its credit agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1842 GMT:\par  \par      Stock indexes              Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            962.45           -0.31\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      1948.99             1.9\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                 96673.40            0.57\par  Mexico IPC                     46873.16            0.28\par  Chile IPSA                      5114.64            -0.4\par  Argentina MerVal              103738.92           3.204\par                                           \par  Colombia COLCAP                 1256.57           -1.25\par                                           \par                                                         \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      5.4045            0.50\par  Mexico peso                     20.5305            1.26\par  Chile peso                        974.2            7.62\par  Colombia peso                    4349.6            3.06\par  Peru sol                         3.8994           -0.20\par  Argentina peso (interbank)     128.2200           -0.16\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (parallel)           290           -0.34\par                                           \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew and Devik Jain in Bengaluru; editing\par by Jonathan Oatis and Richard Chang)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-15T20:35:02