\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  decided to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  with the sale of USD 25 billion to contain the historic rise of the dollar.\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a USD 25 billion program in view of the historic rise of the dollar that has been affecting the country in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  consists of the sale of spot dollars for up to USD 10 billion and the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments for the same amount. "The Council of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile, in order to facilitate the adjustment of the Chilean economy to the uncertain and changing internal and external conditions, has decided to implement a program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and preventive provision of liquidity in dollars, for an amount of up to USD$ 25 billion starting next Monday, July 18 and until September 30, 2022\u8243\'20\'33, communicated the entity.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stated that "the Board considers appropriate to offer, on a precautionary basis, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program for an amount of up to USD 5,000 million. This will be complemented by a liquidity program in pesos through over-the-counter REPO \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same terms".\par \par \uc2 In Chile, the dollar has climbed to historic prices. During this Thursday, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at $1,051 (USD 1.05) and this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is added to the "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " of the beginning of the week when the entity stated that it would implement measures "if necessary".\par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  raised its interest rate by 75 basis points to 9.75%. The agency explained that this decision was applied due to the implications of global inflation and the decision of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  to increase its interest rate by 75 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In a conversation with Infobae, the general manager of Empresas Golden, Wilfredo Araya, commented that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will be carried out in different stages so that the outflow of dollars from the country is gradual", pushing down the value of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Wilfredo Araya explained that one of these stages is the spot sale or instantaneous sale of dollars. "To cope with a rapid fall in the exchange rate is the direct sale of current dollar reserves by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , equivalent to USD 10 billion, which is what is known as spot selling."\par \par \uc2 Another stage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision is the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for another USD 10 billion. The expert explained that "in the general market, different entities such as importers or exporters hedge against risk volatility through contracts such as forward contracts, where I fix the price for a certain period of time with the option of renewing the contract if I wish to continue protecting the exchange rate". In this case, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as counterparty, "would decide to close the contracts and sell the dollar forward contracts. The liquidation of these contracts through the sale of dollars would mean that we would be talking about USD 10 billion". The effect of this would have a short-term impact, but not instantaneous.\par \par \uc2 Finally, for USD 5 billion, a swap program will be carried out, which "in simple terms, is a program regarding the valuation of the dollar as a result of interest rates between connections, or transactions, with different countries". As long as interest rates continue to increase, "the transaction cost gap in different countries, which is known as swap, has a greater increase, and this has an impact on the price". In view of this, what the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would do is "to make a swap program so that this transactional cost of dollars with international entities, international economies, also has a much lower impact".\par \par \uc2 Due to millionaire irregularities, the liquidator of the assets seized from one of Chile's top swindlers is asked to be removed.\par \par \uc2 Chilean parliament will carry out drug test by lottery for deputies and will make the results public\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220715ei7f008aa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
