\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Latin American  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rise and stock markets trade mixed; Chilean peso leads gains\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Jul 15 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded higher on Friday amid reduced investor aversion to risky assets, on a day when the Chilean peso posted strong gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sustained slide.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar consolidated near two-decade highs on Friday as traders flirted with the prospect of a 100 basis point rate hike by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  later this month, while the euro held near parity.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index, which measures the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , retreated about 0.5% after consumer confidence data came in above expectations.\par \par \uc2 * Gains were led by the Chilean peso, which climbed 5.69% to 989.50/989.80 units per dollar. Meanwhile, the leading index of the Santiago Stock Exchange, the IPSA, fell 1.34% to 5,066.57 points.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market for up to 25 billion dollars to prevent possible distortions in the face of the galloping advance of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 * In a statement issued on Thursday night, the agency said that in recent days the peso depreciation has occurred with unusually high intensity and volatility, which stresses the price formation of the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, the Colombian peso gained 1.60% to 4,420 units per dollar, while the stock market's benchmark index, the MSCI COLCAP, lost 0.34% to 1,268.46 points.\par \par \uc2 * The Mexican peso was trading at 20.5990 units per dollar, with a gain of 0.91% against the Reuters reference price on Thursday, but was on track to end the week with a cumulative loss of 1.22%.\par \par \uc2 * From a technical point of view, it is probable that the exchange rate will stabilize around 20.80 pesos per dollar, while awaiting more relevant economic information," said the local firm Banco Base in an analysis note.\par \par \uc2 * The main stock index S&P;/BMV IPC, which comprises the 35 most liquid companies in the Mexican market, gained 0.06% to 46,767.45 units, after the release of better-than-expected retail sales figures in the United States, dispelling some concerns about a recession, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 * The Brazilian real appreciated 0.62% to 5.3910 units per dollar, while the Bovespa index of Sao Paulo's B3 stock exchange lost 0.86% to 95,291.47 points.\par \par \uc2 * In Argentina, the peso was down 0.19% to 128.25 per dollar in depreciation regulated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Merval stock index gained 1.07% to 101,598.10 units, encouraged by the trend of the local Adrs traded in New York, in a cautious business context due to local economic doubts.\par \par \uc2 * There is no mood in the market for the market to take off. There are many doubts and few certainties in the market, that is why the investor prefers to be liquid and covered", said a trader.\par \par \uc2 * The Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, gained 0.64% to 3.863/3.880 units per dollar. Meanwhile, the Lima Stock Exchange benchmark yielded 0.06% to 457.57 points.\par \par \uc2 Quotations at 1438 GMT\par \par \uc2 Indices Price Var pct Var pct\par \par \uc2 daily stock indexes in the year\par \par \uc2 MSCI Emerging Markets\par \par \uc2 965,45 -21,73\par \par \uc2 -0,52\par \par \uc2 MSCI Latin America\par \par \uc2 1.912,59 -8,68\par \par \uc2 -3,03\par \par \uc2 Bovespa Brazil\par \par \uc2 95.974,14 -8,4412\par \par \uc2 -0,15\par \par \uc2 IPC Mexico\par \par \uc2 46.757,9 -12,23\par \par \uc2 0,04\par \par \uc2 Argentina MerVal\par \par \uc2 101.469,73 21,52\par \par \uc2 0,946\par \par \uc2 COLCAP Colombia\par \par \uc2 1.269,52 -9,96\par \par \uc2 -0,23\par \par \uc2 IPSA Chile\par \par \uc2 5.063,79 17,54\par \par \uc2 -1,4\par \par \uc2 Selective Peru\par \par \uc2 457,55 -10,70\par \par \uc2 -0,04\par \par \uc2 Dollar vs. exchange rate Var pct Var pct\par \par \uc2 to monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the year\par \par \uc2 Brazilian real\par \par \uc2 5,3919 3,32\par \par \uc2 -2,53\par \par \uc2 Mexican peso\par \par \uc2 20,5990 -0,52\par \par \uc2 -2,42\par \par \uc2 Chilean peso\par \par \uc2 991,7 -13,82\par \par \uc2 -7,34\par \par \uc2 Colombian peso\par \par \uc2 4.389,6 -7,58\par \par \uc2 -5,62\par \par \uc2 Peruvian sol\par \par \uc2 3,8925 +2,00\par \par \uc2 -2,00\par \par \uc2 Argentine peso\par \par \uc2 128,22 -19,91\par \par \uc2 -2,34\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Froil\u225\'00\'E1n Romero. Additional reporting by Luis Jaime Acosta in Bogota, Walter Bianchi in Buenos Aires and Vicente Valdivia)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220715ei7f007id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
