\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's peso surges as c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Latam\uc2  stocks slide amid China gloom\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par 16:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Susan Mathew\par     July 15 (Reuters) - Chile's peso shot up as much as 6% on\par Friday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from\par record lows, while a pause in the dollar prompted gains in most\par other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on track for its best\par session ever as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  agreed to a $25 billion\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid a rallying dollar.\par     Bets about an aggressive move by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par this month and safe-haven appeal amid recession worries have\par powered the dollar to near two-decade highs.\par     Tumbling prices of copper, Chile's main export revenue item,\par amid worries about falling demand from top metal consumer China,\par have also weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The peso breached 1,060 per dollar for the first time on\par Thursday and has been in record low territory for over three\par weeks. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  move lifted it to 986.30 on Friday.  \par     "The recent sell-off will force \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Chile\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par policymakers to raise policy rates more aggressively and extend\par the tightening cycle. ... As policymakers step up policy\par tightening and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can rebound,"\par said analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Mexico's peso rose 0.3% as the dollar took a breather\par after two of the Fed's most hawkish policymakers said overnight\par they favoured another 75-basis-point hike after hot U.S.\par inflation had raised bets of a 100 bps move this month. \par     As oil prices recovered, crude exporter Colombia's peso\par  firmed 1.3% to 4,425.6, moving further away from record\par lows of 4,658.02 it hit earlier this week.\par     Brazil's real gave up early gains to trade 0.3%\par lower. \par     Stocks in the region fell, in line with broader emerging\par market peers, as recession worries heightened after grim\par economic growth data from China earlier in the day.\par     Losses on Brazil's Bovespa index were led by iron\par ore miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vale\f28 \uc2 \f2  as the steel-making ingredient dipped\par below $100 on pessimism over China demand.\par     Argentina's heavily controlled peso fell 0.2%. A\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bloomberg\f28 \uc2 \f2  report said Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its\par benchmark interest rate at 52%, according to a person with\par direct knowledge of the matter. The decision in not official yet\par and comes as inflation galloped to 64% in the 12 months to June.\par \par     Meanwhile, Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday announced a\par change in its strategy for setting the country's interest rates,\par seeking to achieve positive real interest rates, which is part\par of its credit agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1357 GMT:\par    Stock indexes            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets        959.31    -0.64\par                                       \par  MSCI LatAm                  1911.90    -0.04\par                                       \par  Brazil Bovespa             95432.40    -0.72\par                                       \par  Mexico IPC                 46922.91     0.39\par                                       \par  Chile IPSA                  5061.83    -1.43\par                                       \par  Argentina MerVal                  -        -\par                                       \par  Colombia COLCAP             1266.06    -0.51\par                                       \par                                              \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest    Daily %\par                                       change\par  Brazil real                  5.4469    -0.28\par                                       \par  Mexico peso                 20.7556     0.17\par                                       \par  Chile peso                   1008.1     4.00\par                                       \par  Colombia peso                4425.6     1.29\par  Peru sol                          -        -\par                                       \par  Argentina peso             128.2100    -0.16\par  (interbank)                          \par                                       \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; editing by Jonathan\par Oatis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-15T15:15:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA000002022071