\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Risk aversion hits the financial markets\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Clara Zepeda Peri\u243\'00\'F3dico La JornadaFriday, July 15, 2022, p.23Amid a wave of nervousness about what the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will do in its next monetary meeting, after the surprise inflation figure for June, risk aversion hit risky financial instruments. The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated against the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 0.70 percent, equivalent to 14.48 cents, to close at 20.8254 units per spot dollar. According to \uc2 Banco de M\u233\'00\'E9xico\uc2 , the peso-dollar parity traded between a maximum of 21.0200 units and a minimum of 20.8050 units.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, the DXY, which measures the performance of the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its US counterpart, appreciated 0.68 percent to 108.487 units.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded at 0.9985 dollars per dollar, a new 20-year low, to close at 1.0019 dollars. In the United States, producer inflation in June reached an annual rate of 11.3 percent, above market expectations of 10.7 percent and May producer inflation of 10.9 percent, according to revised figures.\par \par \uc2 The yield on 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds was pressured to 2.96 percent, up 1.93 percent from the previous close; equity markets ended the session mixed, as investors analyzed rate hikes and fears of a recession.\par \par \uc2 As in the rest of the financial markets, oil closed the session with losses. WTI crude fell 0.17 percent to 96.14 dollars per barrel. Brent crude lost 0.02 percent and closed at 99.55 dollars per barrel. The Mexican blend closed at 90.87 dollars.\par \par \uc2 Chilean peso plummetsThe\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the exchange market for 25 billion dollars, in an attempt to halt the record depreciation of the peso, which in the last few days has been unusually intense and volatile. The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has broken downward records, in the last week falling 8.6 percent to 1,051 units per dollar. This is due to the appreciation of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as the fall in the international price of copper, of which Chile is the world's leading producer, the agency explained.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be in force from July 18 to September 30, 2022. A day earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  raised its reference rate to 9.75 percent, amid a scenario of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 From the Editor, with information from Afp\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220715ei7f004gc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
