\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar sets new high in  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  does not rule out  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar remained this Tuesday in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  above 1,000 pesos and reached the historical maximum of 1,026 pesos, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Monday in a statement that it does not rule out taking containment measures.\par \par \uc2 According to local operators, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted between a maximum value of 1,026.43 pesos and a minimum of 996.80 pesos, awaiting the closing of the day.\par \par \uc2 The day before, the Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assured in a statement that the exchange rate "could obstruct the price formation of the exchange market and stress the evolution of other sectors of the financial market".\par \par \uc2 This "would require the Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to ensure the proper functioning of the economy," the report added.\par \par \uc2 Experts blame the escalation of the dollar, which has been at a high for days, on the context of the global strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the fall in the value of copper, the country's main export, due in part to the restrictions that China maintains in several cities due to covid-19.\par \par \uc2 "The price of copper has fallen nearly 20% since the beginning of June, which has generated a deterioration in the terms of trade of our economy" and at the local level "the significant current account deficit, high inflation and uncertainty levels have increased the sensitivity of the economy," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 London Metal Exchange\uc2 , the red metal, of which Chile is the world's main producer, fell to 3.3 dollars per pound on Wednesday, a 3.31% decrease with respect to the previous day and its lowest value in more than a year and a half.\par \par \uc2 Key meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 A key meeting starts this afternoon: the Monetary Policy Meeting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds every month to decide on possible changes in the benchmark interest rate.\par \par \uc2 This rate is already at its highest value since 2001 (9%) after a 75-point increase last June, and on Wednesday it will be known whether or not a new increase will take place in order to contain the inflation that the country is going through.\par \par \uc2 Chile accumulates a 12.5% price increase in 12 months, the highest level since 1994, and according to experts consulted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could close the year at 11%.\par \par \uc2 After a historic GDP rebound of 11.7% in 2021, the largest expansion in four decades, the Chilean economy is showing signs of cooling and estimates of the issuing entity point to GDP growth this year between 1% and 2%. (I)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220712ei7c00cdn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
