\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Concern in Chile over the effects of record dollar prices\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar in Chile suffered a strong rise never seen before, which has awakened concern among experts about the consequences this may have on domestic and foreign trade.\par \par \uc2 The dollar in Chile reached $1,000 for the first time in history and minutes later the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "moderated", dropping to $970. The rise of the North American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was registered around midday on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The day began with the dollar at a value of $959, eight pesos more than last Tuesday's close, and after that it began to rise precipitously, according to the Chilean Electronic Stock Exchange website. At 10:05 a.m., the North American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $963.75 and exactly one hour later it reached $975. However, at 11:22 a.m. it reached $980.65, and a few minutes before 11:40 a.m. it was quoted at $1,000.\par \par \uc2 At the same time that this was happening, the value of copper closed in the red again. Copper is Chile's main export product, and according to the Chilean Copper Commission (Cochilco), the metal was at the price of USD 3.414 per pound, which represents a 3.61% drop. This is the lowest value recorded for this commodity since November 2020.\par \par \uc2 Reactions to the historic rise\par \par \uc2 For Wilfredo Araya, executive director of Empresas Golden, the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "historic" and is consecrated "as a strong resistance in the face of possible new rises". The expert added that these increases would be "justified by the strong fears of a world recession that would start in the United States", which would spread "to the main economies of the world and to the emerging markets".\par \par \uc2 Araya pointed out that in Chile this rise could mean a new increase in the interest rate fixed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its Monetary Policy Meetings. In case the latter happens, "it would bring strong inflationary pressures in our country. With this, it is estimated that the Unidad de Fomento (UF), in the short term, could reach $35,000 (USD 36.05)".\par \par \uc2 The UF is a unit of measurement exclusive to Chile that is used to express the prices of leases, purchase and sale of apartments in Chile. It is also used by Isapres to define their prices to citizens and even by insurance companies to charge their premiums. It is not identified as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but rather "as an indicator of the value of the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is increasing in line with inflation".\par \par \uc2 Finally, Araya emphasized that it is necessary to be attentive "to what will be the decision of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 " of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  and if "there is an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly in the sale of dollars" to "contain the rise in the exchange rate" in the country.\par \par \uc2 Political uncertainty in Chile\par \par \uc2 The rise of the dollar has provoked a debate in Chile. For Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Godoy, head of Analysis of the investment company XTB Latam, the political uncertainty in Chile would also influence the North American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "In domestic matters, political uncertainty has influenced, given by the exit plebiscite, together with the economic uncertainty from the tax reform. This is generating a depreciation effect of the Chilean peso, which in fact, is one of the most depreciated globally and therefore we see an increase in the exchange rate", said Godoy to Emol.com.\par \par \uc2 Another point that has been debated is the possibility that the dollar will officially go above $1,000 in Chile, something that is not so impossible. "The greenback at $1,000 pesos is already a reality and we should not be surprised if we continue to see an uptrend that, both technically and fundamentally, are fully justified," said Renato Campos, chief analyst at Admiral Markets.\par \par \uc2 Finally, Chile's Minister of Finance, \uc2 Mario Marcel\uc2 , called for calm on all sides in the face of this rise. "We must be calm about the fact that factors that in the past made Chile especially vulnerable to the exchange rate are no longer there today, we do not have exchange mismatches in companies or in the financial system that could generate an impact", said the Secretary of State.\par \par \uc2 Chile: former president Ricardo Lagos said that the new Constitution does not have enough consensus\par \par \uc2 Five armed hooded men from a radical Mapuche group destroyed three vehicles in a farm in the south of Chile.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220707ei77008xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
