\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar rises sharply at the open and sets new record high above $940 amid global strengthening of the  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The exchange rate began Tuesday's session under pressure, as has been the trend in recent days, with a jump of $ 12.6 with respect to yesterday's close, standing at $ 940.1 at the opening .\par \par \uc2 The depreciation of the Chilean peso is in line with the global advance of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar index - which measures the greenback against the main world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - expanded by more than 1%. Likewise, the euro, which is one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the greatest weight within this index, succumbs and falls to its lowest level in the last 20 years.\par \par \uc2 The euro falls to a 20-year low against the dollar and parity is only a matter of time.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a global economic recession are once again the main concern among investors, which has increased their appetite for the dollar and turned it into a safe-haven asset.\par \par \uc2 Another factor hitting the Chilean peso is copper. The commodity fell 2.85% on the \uc2 London Metal Exchange\uc2 , reaching US$ 3.541 per pound.\par \par \uc2 According to Cochilco, the downward cycle in the price of the red mineral has been influenced in part by "the risk of recession increased as the rhetoric of aggressive monetary policy rate hikes to reduce inflation in the United States and Europe takes hold in the short term".\par \par \uc2 The Commission recalled on Friday that "during June price dynamics were dominated by global macroeconomic risks and their impact on demand for the metal."\par \par \uc2 XTB Latam's senior analyst, Juan Ortiz, mentioned that "as long as market fears of a recession continue, where analysts and large investment banks are increasingly raising the probability of a recession, we will continue to see falls in the price of the metal and thus directly impact the exchange rate".\par \par \uc2 Under this scenario, the head of research at Capitaria, Ricardo Bustamante, indicated that it is not ruled out that the dollar "could go for new historical highs, in the midst of a further fall in the price of copper". In fact, he did not rule out that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could reach $ 950 under this scenario.\par \par \uc2 He added that "the local uncertainty before the exit plebiscite and due to the proposed tax reform is an additional ingredient that supports the weakening of the peso, generating an additional advance of the dollar in our country".\par \par \uc2 In the same line, the chief analyst of Admiral Markets, Renato Campos, remarked that two months before the exit plebiscite on the proposed new Constitution drafted by the Constitutional Convention, "it generates uncertainty among investors due to its result and the impact it may have on local politics and economy".\par \par \uc2 Bci Estudios recalled in a report sent today to its clients that "the Chilean peso has lost value significantly in the last two months, due to the expectations of important rate increases by central banks of developed countries, especially the Fed, which has led to an outflow of foreign flows".\par \par \uc2 The entity pointed out that "the exchange rate is at its historical maximums and its deviation of variables is close to levels of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding to what has been done by the Treasury".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220705ei750070h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
