\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar opened lower on Tuesday after Treasury  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  and copper rally\b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The exchange rate fell by $10.80 at the opening of trading on Tuesday. The parity was trading at $904.60 at the time of this note after a strong rise of $14.10 on Friday to its historical maximum value ($915.40).\par \par \uc2 Ricardo Bustamante, head of trading studies at Capitaria, stated that the dollar has shown a strong fall at the beginning of the week after last Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , who will sell US$ 5,000 million dollars for two months, with a cap of US$ 200 million per day. "This measure seeks to generate a weakening of the dollar locally, after having approached $920, its highest value in history, amid external and internal factors that supported this rally," he said.\par \par \uc2 "While this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could generate some additional weakening in the short term, close attention to the other fundamentals of the exchange rate, especially copper which has been key in recent times," he warned, adding that "if we see falls in the red metal again due to fears about the global economy, added to local uncertainty as we approach the plebiscite on the new constitution, it is likely that the rises in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon return."\par \par \uc2 Nataly Venegas, FXGlobe market analyst, noted that "internationally this morning it has been flat (0.6%). This is due to the decline in inflation expectations that prompted a reassessment of the outlook for aggressive interest rate hikes, although market volatility dampened a broader decline."\par \par \uc2 At the local level, he specified, "the strong rebound of copper is coupled with the strength of the Chilean peso against the dollar. With a variation of 1.51%, the red metal touched 3.8 usd/lb. This generates bullish expectations, as the market would be assuming the deceleration. In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be carried out by the Treasury in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the next 60 days is considerable (...) In the local market, in terms of volume, US$800 million are traded, so the daily amount to be sold by the Treasury generates pressure for the dollar, taking a bearish path during these two months. It is likely that this morning we will find ourselves with a downward price, towards the $880/$850 areas".\par \par \uc2 Juan Ortiz Godoy, senior market analyst at XTB Latam, believes that the exchange rate will continue its upward trend "where it could seek $900 as a first correction target and at the same time act as support. However, we will have to see the real impact of the Treasury's decision to sell US$ 5 billion to counteract the escalation".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220628ei6s00a8m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
