\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Corbo dismisses CB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  for dollar hike in  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 : "You have to be Tarzan to change its appreciation".\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar continues to rise and climb to new all-time highs. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached $891 early Wednesday morning, affected mainly by the international scenario of rate hikes by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and the slowdown in China due to the impact of the confinements determined by the authorities to contain the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 In spite of this historical rise of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country, the former president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Vittorio Corbo\uc2 , does not see room for the issuing institution to make an exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since he affirms that the appreciation of the dollar is explained by reasons aligned with the fundamentals that move that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "First, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  always studies very carefully if there are misalignments that cannot be explained by its fundamentals, and the second thing is that if it is misaligned, it can be corrected with an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", explained Corbo when participating in the XX Economic Perspectives Seminar "Economic Scenario under Pressure", organized by Sura Inversiones.\par \par \uc2 The economist added that "this is a dollar appreciation problem: you have to be Tarzan to change the appreciation of the dollar, and therefore I see it as unlikely. That is written in the CB's rules. First there has to be a misalignment that cannot be explained by fundamentals, but now there is a rationale that explains the rise of the dollar, which is international appreciation". For this reason, "I see it very unlikely (an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) at this juncture, especially with the uncertainty we are going to have in the coming months. We have to save our ammunition".\par \par \uc2 Rates: "The remedy has to produce effects".In his analysis, Corbo also addressed the problem of inflation, which today stands at 11.5% in twelve months. "Inflation expectations and inflationary compensations in the two-year term continue to be well above the inflation target and those in the 10-year term reach 4.4%. Overheating is still present and indexation mechanisms increase the risk that high inflation becomes more persistent," warned the economist.\par \par \uc2 He pointed out that "to reduce overheating, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been raising the interest rate, this year's Budget reduces public spending by 25% in real terms and no new withdrawals have been approved".\par \par \uc2 In this context, he noted that "the contraction of final demand has affected both private consumption and investment", and said that this factor, together with lower food and fuel price inflation as a result of the global slowdown, "will contribute to reduce inflation".\par \par \uc2 Therefore, he foresees that "new interest rate hikes should be more moderate, to end this cycle at around 9.5% and begin to decline later when inflation begins to move towards the CB's 2% target".\par \par \uc2 Therefore, for Corbo "we are close to the end of the bullish cycle, because the remedy is already in the patient and has to produce its effects. Antibiotics do not have effects when they are just taken, you have to be patient for them to have effects".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220622ei6m008qk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
