\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Saieh and Cueto emerge from bankruptcy and breathe again\b0\par\par\uc2 1,518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Presented by:\par \par \uc2 Good morning and happy Father's Day! Left turn in Colombia: \uc2 Gustavo Petro\uc2  is the new president. It is the first time there has been a leftist president in the history of Colombia. Petro, former mayor of Bogota and former M-19 guerrilla, won almost 51% of the votes. Rodolfo Hern\u225\'00\'E1ndez, the right-wing populist candidate, received almost 47%. Petro has already announced profound reforms and that he would present a tax reform in the first semester of his mandate. This Monday we will see how the market reacts.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the main Latin American foreign investor in Colombia. According to official data, by the end of 2020 there were about 150 Chilean companies, with more than 300 projects in Colombian territory. Investment in the services sector reaches almost US$18 billion.\par \par \uc2 Among the most important: \uc2 Falabella\uc2 , Mallplaza, \uc2 Cencosud\uc2 , \uc2 Parque Arauco\uc2 , Sodimac, Copec, \uc2 CCU\uc2 , Banm\u233\'00\'E9dica, LarrainVial and \uc2 Latam Airlines\uc2 , in addition to the startups NotCo, Cornershop, Houm and Global66.\par \par \uc2 1 1- SAIEH AND CUETO, EMERGING FROM BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 What happened. This week CorpGroupBanking and \uc2 Latam\uc2  finally emerged from bankruptcy in the United States. They are two of the largest defaults in recent history, and they highlighted some of the weaknesses of the institutional framework of the Chilean financial system versus that of Wall Street, by leaving local creditors -including some AFPs- in unequal conditions vis-\u224\'00\'E0-vis foreign creditors. They are two of the biggest local victims of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The exit from default gives air to two of the largest business groups of the last 30 years: Alvaro Saieh, controller of CorpGrup, and the Cueto family, controllers of \uc2 Latam\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If you want to continue reading, subscribe to El Semanal and join our community.\par \par \uc2 2 2- THE \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2 'S DILEMMA: TO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\uc2  OR NOT TO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO HELP THE PESO\par \par \uc2 Is it time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? This is the question the market is beginning to ask. On Friday, the Chilean dollar broke the $870 barrier and registered a record high. The main factors are the Federal Reserve rate hike, the fall in the price of copper, the persistence of fears of a possible recession and the political uncertainty surrounding the text of the new Constitution.\par \par \uc2 When was the last time the \uc2 CB\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was in December 2019, when there was an exchange rate misalignment of around 15%, according to the BCI. In a report, published on Friday, the research department headed by Sergio Lehmann estimates that the conditions for an exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not yet in place, although the alarm sounds that the local and external economic scenario "may exert an inordinate pressure on the Chilean peso and deliver arguments for some exchange measure".\par \par \uc2 But some economists warn that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have sufficient reserves to be able to have an impact.\par \par \uc2 Scotiabank's chief economist warned on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account over the weekend: "With International Reserves at a modest 15% of GDP, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a limited backbone for a massive and successful \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if CLP quickly approaches $900. Keep raising the rate for now and 'pray' that a USD sale is not necessary.\par \par \uc2 3 3- THE AFP DEPLOY THEIR LOBBY IN WASHINGTON\par \par \uc2 What happened. This week Christian Larra\u237\'00\'EDn, the Undersecretary of Social Security, in a series of meetings with some AFPs and their controllers in the United States (Cuprum and Provida), told them that they will not be part of the new system. He informed them that they will not be able to participate in the administration of the future contribution, nor in the additional contribution defined by the reform (6 additional points, to reach 16%, would be the figure). In the next few days, Larra\u237\'00\'EDn will meet with \uc2 AFP H\u225\'00\'E1bitat\uc2 , controlled by the Chilean Chamber of Construction, and Prudential, another financial giant from the United States.\par \par \uc2 Christian Larra\u237\'00\'EDn, with his statement, definitely set off the alert of the international controllers of the AFPs, who at any moment announce the beginning of the process of searching for international law firms to explore legal avenues to protect their investments. Industry sources assure that they have already contacted the ambassador in Washington, Juan Gabriel Vald\u233\'00\'E9s.\par \par \uc2 If you want to continue reading, subscribe to El Semanal and join our community.\par \par \uc2 4 4- GRAPHIC OF THE WEEK: ABOUT WINDOWS\par \par \uc2 Ecological or not? The controversy that erupted due to the government's decision to close Ventanas puts into discussion whether Chile is a State concerned about the environment. And for that you have to look at the ranking of the countries with the best and worst environmental performance. In blue, the 50 countries with the best environmental score in the world, according to the index published by \uc2 Yale University\uc2  in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Chile ranks 44th in the world and the highest in Latin America. The Yale report highlights Chile's remarkable improvement in the last 10 years, aligning itself with the UN Social Development Goals. What is most applauded is the energy transition.\par \par \uc2 If you want to continue reading, subscribe to El Semanal and join our community.\par \par \uc2 A message from the AFP Association For more information click on the image\par \par \uc2 How to increase savings to improve pensions?\par \par \uc2 Several proposals aim to strengthen pension savings, but not all of them are sufficiently effective. Increasing the contribution rate to 18% would have the biggest impact: 80% higher pensions. The birth bonus would increase pension savings: pensions would rise by 58.5%. 5 In this extensive interview, the director of Fundaci\u243\'00\'F3n Chile and founder of Observatorio Fiscal, points out that the new political cycle is generating spaces to discuss how to reform capitalism so that it remains a legitimate alternative as an economic model.\par \par \uc2 To see the full interview, click here or on the image.\par \par \uc2 6 6- NO TACOS OR COBARTAS\par \par \uc2 -The legal problems of BUK, the next Chilean unicorn. This company, known for being one of the main human resources management tools, in 2021 ranked as the third Chilean startup with the highest value, after Cornershop and NotCo.\par \par \uc2 The controversy erupted after acquiring CTRL IT, an attendance control software company, which allowed it to complete its comprehensive service offering and catapulted its exit to the capital market in the United States, where it managed to raise US$ 50 million, reaching a record valuation in a Series A in the history of Latin American startups. Today it has a valuation of at least US$ 417 million.\par \par \uc2 If you want to keep reading, subscribe to El Semanal and join our community.\par \par \uc2 -Side effect. The economist of the University of Chile, Alfonso Vergara, affirms that the credit lines that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended to the banks during the pandemic became a subsidy. This is the almost US$ 40 billion in credit lines of the Conditional Financing Facility for the Increase of Placements (FCIC), which the issuing entity gave to the banks in 2020 in pesos.\par \par \uc2 Subsidized rate. The cost of 0.5% nominal annual rate, which was the TPM, which by the BCCH's own definition was at its technical minimum. Today, according to Vergara's calculations, the banks owe the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  US$ 35,000 million, maturing in 2024, with the subsidized interest rate. This, while the public and companies are being charged market rates, which have been rising over the last year. This has translated into unexpected margins and profits for the banks. The implicit subsidy would be at least US$ 8 billion. The banks' response. They claim that it is not correct to say that the FCIC is a subsidy to the banks. They add that an important part of the credit line was conditioned to the delivery of new credits and that the industry complied. They also refute the figures and emphasize that the banks granted new loans, fulfilling a markedly countercyclical role that alleviated the impact of the crisis.\par \par \uc2 7 7- AGENDA FOR THE WEEK\par \par \uc2 -On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published the minutes of the June Monetary Policy Meeting (MPM), in which the Monetary Policy Rate (MPR) was increased by 75 basis points to 9%. This was what the market anticipated, so the focus will be on what they discussed about the pace of hikes in the future. In the June Monetary Policy Report (IPoM), the \uc2 CB\uc2  expects the annual variation of the CPI to continue increasing, to values slightly above 12% in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 8 8- RECOMMENDATION OF THE WEEK: THE ECONOMIST AND THE NEW CONSTITUTION\par \par \uc2 This week's Economist has a 10-page report on Latin America and its vicious circle of economic stagnation, social frustration and political decay, and how this should matter more to the Western world.\par \par \uc2 He points out that economic stagnation, popular frustration and polarized politics reinforce each other.\par \par \uc2 And he stops to talk about \uc2 Gabriel Boric\uc2 's government and the debate over the new Constitution.\par \par \uc2 He says that Boric is imprisoned between a left that is too utopian, populist and anti-capitalist, and a right that defends monopolies and privileges, with a center that disappeared.\par \par \uc2 Presented by:\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220620ei6k007w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
