\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazilian real snaps three-day rally; eyes weekly gains\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2021\par 16:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil's real outperforms peers for the week\par     * Chilean peso tracks sharpest weekly decline since August\par 2020\par     * Latam stocks index set to fall for the week\par \par     By Shreyashi Sanyal\par     Jan 15 (Reuters) - Brazil's real bucked a three-day winning\par streak on Friday after data showed the first decline in retail\par sales in seven months, although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is set to\par outperform its Latin American peers for the week on improving\par risk sentiment.   \par     The real fell 1% against the dollar as\par official figures showed Brazilian retail sales surprisingly fell\par in November mainly driven by a sizeable fall in sales of food\par products.    \par     "The survey breakdown suggests that those components that\par were performing well during the peak of the pandemic are now\par contracting (food/beverages/supermarket or furniture/home\par appliances), while others components that were more negatively\par affected during that period keep recovering (apparel or cars),"\par Citi strategists wrote in a note.\par     Global risk sentiment showed signs of improving early in the\par week, which has put the real on track to cap the week with gains\par of 2.6%. \par     However, a travel ban imposed by Britain over a Brazilian\par variant of the coronavirus hurt the mood on Friday.\par     The MSCI's index for Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  was set to end the week higher, adding 1.3%. \par     Most risky assets have gained this week on anticipation of a\par faster pace of global economic recovery as COVID-19 vaccines\par start to roll out across the world. Sentiment was also boosted\par by hopes of a fiscal boost from a $1.9 trillion U.S. stimulus\par plan.  \par     The Mexican peso fell 0.6% on Friday, but was set for\par its sharpest weekly gain in nearly one month on improving\par economic data points.\par     Among weekly decliners, Chile's peso led the descent\par to tumble over 3% for the week. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced\par during the week a plan to purchase $12 billion over the next 15\par months to replenish and expand foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par     However, analysts expect substantial near-term weakness in\par the peso, despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dropped 1.2% in early trading. \par     Oil-exporter Colombia's peso fell 0.5% and was also\par set to drop for the week tracking losses in crude prices.\par     Equities across emerging markets fell on Friday, with the\par MSCI's index for Latin American stocks set for\par weekly declines of 1.6%. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1455 GMT:\par     \par  Stock                             Latest   Daily %\par    indexes                                  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets             1360.58  -0.74\par                                             \par  MSCI LatAm                        2500.64  -1.81\par                                             \par  Brazil Bovespa                    121392.  -1.69\par                                    76       \par  Mexico IPC                        45793.9  -0.6\par                         