\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  highlights  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  measures and rules out inflationary pressures\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A positive vision has \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  international reserve replenishment and expansion program. While the announcement generated a sharp depreciation of the Chilean peso and the investment bank sees no signs of a widespread and persistent uptick in inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that the measure is necessary to strengthen Chile's external mattresses, particularly in light of the post-protest experience of October 2019, which led to an unprecedented weakening of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso, which required strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The announcement of the dollar purchase plan raised doubts about the direction inflation could take, in the face of a possible sustained rise in the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose $15 following the announcement of the BC, then closed today's trades with a drop of $13.34 to $728.5.\par \par \uc2 However, the investment bank believes that "negative surprises" in economic data, coupled with sustained progress in coronavirus contagions, would keep inflation levels under pressure, following the uptick at the end of last year.\par \par \uc2 "We still see no signs of a widespread and persistent uptick in inflationary pressures. Domestic activity has been negatively surprised in recent months, and the imposition of new social restraint measures to counteract the increase in new cases of COVID is likely to affect recovery in the short term. So while inflation has surprised considerably upwards, the expectation that the output gap could close by the end of 2022 has probably remained virtually unchanged," goldman Sachs says.\par \par \uc2 Second withdrawal from AFPsThe investment bank emphasized that the uptick in inflation at the end of 2020 is explained only by transitional factors: rising consumption as a result of the first and second withdrawals of 10% of pension funds.\par \par \uc2 In this regard, Goldman estimates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains current monetary policy, at least throughout 2021. However, he emphasized that a scenario of greater control of the coronavirus could lead to a shift towards normalization.\par \par \uc2 "We hope that the Committee will continue to signal the maintenance of the current monetary policy stance until the end of 2021. However, positive news of COVID vaccination efforts and a possible decrease in new infections may begin to change the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assessment towards an earlier normalization of the policy stance," Goldman concludes.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210115eh1e000gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
