\par\par \b \uc2 New Chile Constitution Could Give State Bigger Economic Role -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2020\par 19:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1346 ET - Chile will hold a referendum on Sunday to write a new constitution, which could "entrench greater state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. That could help \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy recover faster than others in Latin America; however, the constitution-writing process is also expected to fuel uncertainty, the firm says. "Political uncertainty is now the main certainty in Chile," it says. "Sunday's landmark referendum on constitutional change could be the start of a long and complex process to alter its political landscape." If the referendum is approved, Chileans will elect in April the assembly that will write the charter. (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1128 ET - \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep interest rates on hold in the short term as the ruble's weakness feeds through to higher inflation, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. Further interest-rate cuts are "off the table" for as long as inflation continues to rise toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4% target and the ruble remains "on the back foot," Capital Economics economist Liam Peach says. However, inflation will peak in the coming months and begin to fall in the first half of 2021, prompting the bank to cut rates by 25 basis points in February, he says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its policy rate at 4.25% Friday. USD/RUB last trades down 0.5% at 76.2478. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1047 ET - U.S. and eurozone third quarter economic growth figures due next week are viewed as backward looking so will probably have a limited impact on the euro-dollar exchange rate, \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  says. Other data scheduled in coming days including durable goods orders, consumer confidence, personal income and personal consumption expenditure in the U.S. and the ifo's German business climate index will have a "greater impact" on EUR/USD, \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  's Roberto Mialich says. The German business climate index is likely to show a "renewed decline" in business confidence, which should "curb any further EUR/USD rally much beyond 1.18 for now," he says. EUR/USD rises 0.1% to 1.1830. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1044 ET - The world economy has recovered about 60% of the output lost in the first half of the year, but recoveries in most parts of the world have already slowed and prospects now vary according to countries' success in controlling the virus, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. "The outlook for Europe has darkened as second waves have prompted new restrictions and fiscal support is being scaled back," says the forecasting firm. The U.S. looks more resilient, with risks in both directions relating to the virus and to the possibility of post-election fiscal stimulus. Inflation will stay very low everywhere, implying that the era of unprecedented monetary policy support is set to continue for at least the next couple of years, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1041 ET - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's October 29 policy meeting is unlikely to materially impact the euro as further stimulus measures aren't expected until the end of the year, \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  says. "[\uc2 ECB\uc2  ] President \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  is expected to delay the announcement of further monetary policy expansion--in the form of more asset purchases under the pandemic emergency purchase program facility--to the final Monetary Policy Committee meeting of 2020 on December 10," \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  's Roberto Mialich says. EUR/USD rises 0.2% to 1.1839.(renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 ET - The absence of an increase in global risk aversion has stopped the euro and sterling from falling considerably against the dollar despite rising coronavirus cases and Brexit risks, \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  says. Given the second coronavirus wave and the threat of a no-deal Brexit, "one might have imagined" EUR/USD and GBP/USD would fall towards 1.16 and below 1.28, respectively, "if not further," \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  's Roberto Mialich says. The "resilience" the two exchange rates reflects the dollar's role as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. The dollar has "lost momentum" recently on hopes for another U.S. fiscal stimulus package and news that Brexit negotiations will continue until mid-November. EUR/USD rises 0.1% to 1.1833 and GBP/USD falls 0.2% to 1.3059. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0933 ET - Spain has replaced Mexico as the most vulnerable economy in the world to Covid-19, according to Oxford Economics. After Spain and Mexico, the Philippines, the U.S., and Brazil rank as the most vulnerable economies. On the other hand, economies like Switzerland, Australia, New Zealand and Mongolia remain the least vulnerable. "The global economy has become more vulnerable to Covid-19 with a 30% of growth in new cases since August," says Evghenia Sleptsova, senior economist at the forecasting firm. Big parts of the Northern Hemisphere are being afflicted by the second wave of the pandemic and this has far outweighed some improvements in epidemiology in some emerging markets, such as Brazil and India, Sleptsova says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 ET - A new U.S. administration under Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  may hurt the \uc2 U.K. government\uc2  's chances of agreeing a trade deal with the U.S. any time soon, as President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has backed the U.K. leaving the EU and emboldened the Brexit movement, Frederique Carrier at \uc2 RBC Wealth Management\uc2  says. Although Biden's position is less well known, the Obama administration opposed preferential trade terms for a U.K. "out of Europe," she says. Moreover, given the size of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  compared with the size of the U.K., Biden is unlikely to prioritize a U.K. trade deal. With U.S.-U.K. free trade deal talks on hold until spring because of the pandemic, Biden could pause all negotiations while re-examining U.S. trade policy, Carrier says. (anthony.orunagoriainoff@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 ET - \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is unlikely to cut its main interest rate further, despite similar considerations under way at the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  -- which traders tend to think of as Canada's antipodal twin, senior economists at CIBC Capital Markets tell clients. \uc2 CIBC\uc2  says clients have inquired about another \uc2 BOC\uc2  rate cut, or even negative rates, given \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is setting stage for another cut next month. "It's clear to us that the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  , having passed over the opportunity to go below 0.25% when the economy was in even more dire straits in the spring, believes that lower rates ... would not be helpful," firm says. It adds \uc2 BOC\uc2  Gov. \uc2 Tiff Macklem\uc2  has been forthright that negative rates are not under active consideration. (paul.vieira@wsj.com, @paulvieira)\par \par \uc2 0835 ET - Economists at \uc2 PNC Financial Services\uc2  advise clients the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  's main interest rate will remain as is until 2024, arguing that is the time required to absorb the spare economic capacity the pandemic has created. \uc2 BOC\uc2  Gov. \uc2 Tiff Macklem\uc2  said in July he expects the benchmark rate, of 0.25%, to remain unchanged for at least two years. PNC said Canada's recovery will unfold in "fits and starts" after a rapid upswing in growth in 3Q, likely 40%-plus at an annual rate. Despite heavy dose of government stimulus, PNC said the economy will face stiff headwinds. For instance, it expects demand for energy to slow, and renewable power to eat into market share from conventional sources. It does not expect GDP to return to prepandemic levels until 2023. (paul.vieira@wsj.com; @paulvieira)\par \par \uc2 0809 ET - The outlook for sterling remains grim due to the U.K.'s large budget deficit, weak economic activity and the prospect of worse trade conditions with EU next year, \uc2 MUFG Bank\uc2  says. Noting the \uc2 U.K. government\uc2  's announcement Thursday of fresh stimulus measures in response to coronavirus, \uc2 MUFG\uc2 's \uc2 Derek Halpenny\uc2  says the nation's budget deficit looks set to become the worst or "very close" to the worst among advanced economies. Furthermore, rising coronavirus cases underlines the prospect of a renewed contraction in real inflation-adjusted gross domestic product in the fourth quarter while there is still a "way to go yet" in Brexit negotiations, he says. GBP/USD falls 0.1% to 1.3067 and EUR/GBP rises 0.3% to 0.9064. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0803 ET - The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's decision to leave interest rates unchanged Thursday could prove particularly costly if Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wins November's U.S. election, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. "The risk that the U.S. may impose sanctions on Turkey for purchasing the Russian S-400s air defence system would increase," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  's \uc2 Piotr Matys\uc2  says. To "some extent" the prospect of a Biden victory is already in the price but USD/TRY could still rise beyond the psychological level of 8.00, he says. USD/TRY rose to an all-time high of 7.9792 Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its one-week repo rate at 10.25%, surprising many analysts who expected a rate rise. USD/TRY last trades up 0.3% at 7.9634. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 23, 2020 13:46 ET (17:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020201023egan003em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
