\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real on a tear despite bleak outlook; Latam stocks gain\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2020\par 21:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil's real at near two-month high\par     * Stocks rise as U.S., China services data brews optimism\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso falls; C.bank to scale back NDF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew and Ambar Warrick\par     June 3 (Reuters) - Brazil's real surged on Wednesday after\par industrial output in the country fell less than expected, while\par Latin American stocks surged as major global economies were seen\par recovering from the coronavirus' economic rout. \par     The real rose 2.4% to a near two-month high as\par industrial production in Brazil fell 18.8% in April at its\par fastest pace on record due to coronavirus containment measures,\par but the drop was less than the estimated 29.2% slide.\par  \par     "It still highlights that GDP will fall dramatically in Q2 \u8211\'20\'13\par perhaps by 10%-12% quarter on quarter," said William Jackson,\par chief emerging markets economist at Capital Economics.\par     "It will also provide (the monetary policy committee) with\par plenty of reason to cut interest rates further later this\par month."\par     The real has been one of the worst-performing emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, but a recent bout of risk appetite\par has lifted it from record lows, even as pandemic and political\par woes persist.\par     Hopes of a broader economic recovery gained momentum as\par readings showed business activity in the United States and China\par beginning to recover. \par     Sao Paulo listed stocks extended gains to a fourth\par session with financials serving as the biggest boost to the\par Bovespa. \par     Most other Latam stocks also rose, tracking Wall Street\par higher as the U.S. job market was also seen stabilizing.\par     Chile's peso rose 1.3% after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would gradually scale back its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program in the non-deliverable forward (NDF) market\par amid lower peso volatility.\par     One-month NDFs on the peso were trading at\par 770.31 to the dollar by 1902 GMT, compared with the spot rate of\par 770.30.\par      The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said it was speaking with its U.S.\par and Chinese counterparts to broaden the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lines.\par     Argentina's debt restructuring saga continued. A prominent\par group of the country's creditors said its restructuring proposal\par was in line with an \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  assessment of\par what would be sustainable and called for a deal to help the\par country avoid a costly default. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     \par     Stock indexes             Latest      Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          986.88                2.01\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    1972.30                 3.7\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa               92953.76                2.09\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   38113.68                1.74\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    3813.97                 1.7\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             43911.26               4.457\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1151.94                3.06\par                                         \par                                                           \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest      Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.0852                2.43\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   21.7550                0.12\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      770.3                1.29\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3606.37                0.60\par  Peru sol                       3.4017               -0.21\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                68.8000               -0.12\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Alistair Bell and Lisa Shumaker)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-6-3T20:37:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200603eg6303e82\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
