\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Minute by minute Santiago Stock Exchange records its baddest month since 1998 and January-March becomes the worst quarter in history\b0\par\par\uc2 9,510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 17:18 The Santiago Stock Exchange ended well a month and a quarter for forgetting as a result of social outporhus, economic slowdown and, above all, coronavirus. See. IpSA said goodbye to \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a strong jump of 5.17%, its fifth consecutive hike. However, in March, marked by the scouring of the pandemic in the markets, the index contracted 15.4%. This is the worst monthly performance since August 1998. But everything can be worse. In the January-March balance sheet, the indicator accumulates a drop of 25.32%, its worst historical quarterly performance.\par \par \uc2 14:00 Dollar rises against Chilean peso and closes with the highest quarterly rise in history\par \par \uc2 11:52 The Santiago Stock Exchange folds into this trend and is heading towards its fifth consecutive rise. The IPSA of the Santiago Stock Exchange jumps 3.88% right now. Retail pushes the selective force hard. \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  rises 8.14%, while Falabella rises 7.98%.\par \par \uc2 11:40 U.S. stocks started the day with moderate casualties, but then reversed that trend and at this time they settled in the blue numbers. The dow Jones industrial average rises 0.62%, while S&P 500 shares climb 0.17%. The tech index, meanwhile, jumps 1.35%.\par \par \uc2 08:52 The dollar is quoted at $854, 50 in early trades in the local stock market, a hike of $1.96 compared to yesterday's close.\par \par \uc2 08:44 Oil price rebounds from 18-year lows over possible negotiation between Putin and Trump\par \par \uc2 08:06 Gold prices fall 1% from the dollar's rise and behind