 of a month in extreme negative for markets due to theCoronavirus. The selective completes its fourth consecutive hike, a period in which it accumulates a jump of 14.6%. Cap (9.38%), SQM B (7.97%) and SQM A (+6.45%) were the most prominent actions of the day.\par \par \uc2 15:40 European stocks closed with profits on Monday after a last-minute hike, with purchases focusing mainly on the defensive sectors amid falling oil prices and continued anxiety about coronavirus. The pan-European STOXX 600 index closed with an increase of 1.1% after falling about 1% earlier in the day. A solid opening on Wall Street, spurred by optimism about the fight against the economic impact of the outbreak, backed the market at the end of the European session (Reuters).\par \par \uc2 13:56 Dollar exits the initial lethargy and shoots after four falls in a row against Chilean peso\par \par \uc2 11:06 Las Bolsa de Santiago has a vigorous start. The IPSA, the main index of the local square, rises, 2.67% at the moment.\par \par \uc2 10:50 Wall Street experiences timid hikes in the first \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the day, in an attempt to recover from Monday's bulging losses. Precisely, experts said, there are many opportunity purchases at the start of the day. These rises occur despite the fear of quarantine extensions to try to moderate the coronavirus spread curve, especially after President Donald Trump recommended extending social restraint until April 30. In that context, the Dow Jones rises 0.44%, while the S&P 500 scales 1.31%. \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  shares climb 0.95%.\par \par \uc2 09:10 Copper futures down 0.23% to $2,1670 per pound\par \par \uc2 08:50 The dollar starts the session with a slight increase of $2.32 and settles on the $837.70 seller\par \par \uc2 08:20 \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  projects S&P 500 company dividends would fall 25% in 2020\par \par \uc2 07:38 The shares of Italian football club Juventus experienced a clear rise on Monday on Monday on the 