\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Chile's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  doesn't expect technical recession, it will avoid panic around the peso: vice president\b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones\par \par \uc2 LONDON, 22 Jan (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly if violent protests again threaten the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso, though it hopes the relative calm of recent weeks will be enough to keep the country out of a recession, he said the body's vice president, Joaqu\u237\'00\'EDn Vial.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Reuters, Vial said the biggest protests since Chile's 1990 return to democracy had caused serious damage to the economy.\par \par \uc2 However, he believes the situation will not be worse than what the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  feared in December when it cut its growth forecast for 2020 to a range of 0.5%-1.5% from an earlier 2.75%-3.75%.\par \par \uc2 "It seems to me that the estimate we made last quarter is very much in line with what happened," Vial said.\par \par \uc2 Asked if there was still the risk of a "technical" recession, defined as consecutive quarterly contractions in the economy, he added that "if you look at the graph, we're probably going to avoid it because the worst figures were in October and November."\par \par \uc2 (Edited in Spanish by Natalia Ramos/Gabriela Donoso)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200122eg1m004b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
