\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Geopolitical tensions weigh on Latam markets, Chile peso outperforms\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2020\par 20:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew\par     Jan 7 (Reuters) - Latin American stocks weakened on Tuesday\par because of lingering uncertainty around a standoff between the\par United States and Iran, while Chile's peso outperformed\par following a sharp sell-off in the previous session.\par     Regional stock indices fell between 0.2% and 0.9%. Brazil\par stocks posted their fifth losing session in six. An index of\par global stocks traded flat with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par index and the S&P 500 declining.\par     The killing of a top Iranian general by the United States on\par Friday has made investors cautious as they wait to see how this\par latest dent in Washington-Tehran relations would play out as\par Iran vowed retaliation. \par     "Local assets are being driven by external drivers,\par specifically the uptick in geopolitical risk and a stronger\par dollar," said Gustavo Rangel, chief economist, LATAM at ING New\par York.\par     The dollar gained momentum as a rally in the Japanese yen\par and the Swiss franc - safe havens that have been favored since\par the rise in U.S.-Iran tensions - faded, while\par better-than-expected U.S. non-manufacturing sector and factory\par orders data provided an additional boost.\par     Brazil's real and Mexico's peso traded flat,\par while Colombia's peso, sensitive to oil prices on account\par of being an exporter, fell half a percent for its biggest\par one-day fall in six weeks, as crude prices slipped. \par     The Chilean peso, meanwhile, firmed 0.4% after two\par days of heavy losses. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost almost 3% thanks in part\par to a fall in copper prices on Monday and as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par suspended \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market this\par week.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had set up foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that were to last until May 2020 after the peso\par hit an all-time low in November following violent protests over\par inequality.\par     Copper prices also tend to have significant sway on the peso\par as the base metal is Chile's largest export. \par     On Tuesday, the state copper agency said output slumped at\par state miner Codelco and BHP's sprawling Escondida mine in\par November amid riots. Copper prices on the London's Metals\par Exchange closed higher.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said export revenue crept up in\par December, despite a fall in the value of copper shipments. The\par head of Chile's mining trade union on Tuesday said copper price\par is unlikely to rebound in 2020 even if trade tensions between\par the United States and China subside.\par     Santiago's IPSA stock index rose 0.6% to its\par highest in more than two months.\par     \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1931 GMT:\par     Stock indexes             Latest    Daily %\par                                          change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1116.59      0.36\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2929.11     -0.65\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              116696.55     -0.16\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   44106.05     -0.87\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    4913.52       0.6\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             41140.16    -0.795\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1665.05     -0.68\par                                         \par                                                 \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest    Daily %\par                                          change\par  Brazil real                    4.0610      0.06\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   18.8700     -0.17\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      768.8      0.48\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                    3261     -0.51\par  Peru sol                        3.321      0.09\par                                         \par  Argentine peso                 59.730     -0.16\par                                         \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; editing by Grant\par McCool)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-7T20:58:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200107eg17035np\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
