\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's historic  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  fails to curb peso volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A day after \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a historic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the depreciation of the peso, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday suffered a day of heavy volatility. The $20 billion injected by the autonomous body on Thursday has not calmed the markets, but there has been some recovery from the peso to the dollar. If the record of 828 pesos per greenback was reached on Thursday, it closed at 809 today. During the day the depreciation left him at times in 797 with peaks of up to 826. And it was precisely the movements of the peso against the dollar that caused the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take the action.\par \par \uc2 "The origin of this increased uncertainty is a growing and persistent degree of crispness in the country, expressed in public security issues, in political conflicts, in questioning and weakening of the institutions," the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Mario Marcel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The economist said they aspire to reduce volatility\u8212\'20\'14in fact, he has announced that he will inject 2,000 of the $20 billion between Monday and Friday\u8212\'20\'14but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures will not be able to influence the origins of uncertainty: "It is clear that when we see in the economy a growing degree of uncertainty that influences certain markets, particularly those that are more sensitive to it, as in this case the exchange market, of course we can through measures like this reduce volatility, contain some of that uncertainty, but we have no ability to influence the origins of it."\par \par \uc2 For Economy Minister Lucas Palacios, "the dollar continues with volatility because markets remain very speculative regarding the economic situation in our country." On the injection of $20 billion, he indicated that it is a "very significant amount, corresponding to roughly half of the international reserves held by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on the rise since the start of demonstrations on 18 October in Chile, which in addition to peaceful protests has caused violent altercations in different cities of the country. At the moment, there is no clear way out of the conflict. Neither social measures nor the possibility of changing the Constitution seem sufficient to calm the street, and the political crisis has already spread the economy to high levels of uncertainty. If on 18 October the dollar was changed to 712 Chilean pesos, in mid-November it exceeded the barrier of 800, marking unprecedented levels.\par \par \uc2 The last time the Chilean autonomous body had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the exchange rate market was in 2011, however, it is the largest such \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the flexible exchange rate system debuted in Chile in 1999. The new and historic injection will be applied from next Monday until May 29. The agency will report every Friday the amount, terms and conditions of the auctions.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191130efbu001d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
