\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  will  \highlight22\uc2 intervene foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market in the face of weakness in weight\b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 28 Nov (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with asset sales of up to $20 billion, amid the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crash over the country's social uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed Thursday in its second consecutive all-time low, in a volatile session in the face of the wave of protests shaking the country more than 40 days ago. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take place from Monday and will be extended until May next year.\par \par \uc2 "The events in our country in recent weeks have affected the normal functioning of the economy," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The program will consist of a possible sale of $10 billion in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and up to another $10 billion in sales of "exchange hedging instruments".\par \par \uc2 "This exceptional measure is consistent with the monetary policy scheme, based on an inflationary goal and exchange rate flexibility," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement added.\par \par \uc2 At least 26 people have been killed, more than 13,000 injured and 25,000 have been arrested in Chile amid demonstrations, rants and incendiary attacks on supermarkets, metro stations, hotels and churches.\par \par \uc2 The bank is expected to cut its benchmark interest rate to 1.5% in December, according to a monthly analyst survey published on November 12, at a time when the riots are affecting the copper-producing country's growth.\par \par \uc2 (Report of Fabian Cambero. Edited by Rodrigo Charme)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191129efbt004r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
