\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexican peso higher after rate cut, Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls for 9th session\b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2019\par 21:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cuts interest rates by 25 bps \par     * Chile peso hits new low as unrest continues\par     * Latam stocks pulled higher on gains from Bovespa \par \par  (Updates prices, adds \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexico \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision, comment)\par     By Medha Singh\par     Nov 14 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso reversed course on\par Thursday to trade higher after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexico's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered\par borrowing costs for the third time this year, while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso\par hit fresh record lows despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A divided \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut interest rates by 25 basis points to\par 7.50%, in line with the consensus forecast of a Reuters poll of\par analysts published earlier this week, but flagged growth risks\par for Mexico, Latin America's second largest economy.\par     The peso, which had slid about 1% in the run-up to\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision, moved higher.\par     Two of the bank's five-member board voted to cut rates by 50\par basis points.\par     "The easing cycle will continue until next year until the\par overnight rate is 6.25% by the end of 2020," said Gabriela Soni,\par chief investment officer for Mexico at UBS Global Wealth\par Management.      \par     "We do, however, recognize that monetary policy could be\par less effective as uncertainty about the domestic economic\par policy, increasing violence, and security problems will continue\par weighing on investment decisions."\par     Mexico narrowly escaped sliding into recession in the first\par half of 2019, and preliminary figures showed that gross domestic\par product inched forward by just 0.1% in the third quarter. \par     MSCI's index tracking Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  eyed its ninth consecutive session of declines\par as broader risk sentiment took a hit from weak economic data out\par of major global economies such as China and the Eurozone.\par     Brazil's real and Colombia's peso fell between\par 0.5% and 0.7%, while the Chilean peso tumbled another 1%\par to hit a fresh all-time low, despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  injecting\par $4 billion into the financial system on Thursday to boost\par liquidity.\par     The country has been hit by weeks of protests that have hurt\par investor confidence.\par     "Markets were hoping that (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) would stabilize the\par Chilean peso and instead we broke through a key psychological\par level of 800," said Paresh Upadhyaya, director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategy at Amundi Pioneer Investments.\par     Stocks in the region were pulled slightly\par higher by heavyweight Brazil's Bovespa. \par     Shares in Via Varejo rose 7% after the retailer\par said an in-house investigation into alleged accounting\par irregularities has not uncovered anything so far.\par     Stocks in Chile were up 1.3% but still on track to\par lose nearly 5% for the week.\par         \par   Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2024 GMT: \par  Stock indexes                    Latest     daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            1042.20    -0.16\par                                              \par  MSCI LatAm                       2659.50    0.22\par                                              \par  Brazil Bovespa                   106423.97  0.34\par  Mexico IPC                       43086.41   -0.03\par  Chile SPIPSA                     4498.52    1.96\par  Argentina MerVal                 31019.69   -4.085\par  Colombia IGBC                    13190.43   -0.4\par                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        Latest     daily % change\par  Brazil real                      4.1855     -0.38\par  Mexico peso                      19.3240    0.13\par  Chile peso                       803.8      -1.11\par  Colombia peso                    3450       -0.73\par                                              \par  Peru sol                         3.387      0.03\par  Argentina peso (interbank)       59.6950    0.06\par                                              \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Medha Singh and Agamoni Ghosh in Bengaluru;\par Additional reporting by Kate Duguid in New York, Editing by\par Rosalba O'Brien)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-11-14T21:58:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191114efbe04it5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
