\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weakens on growth fears, rate cut expected in Mexico\b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2019\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Chile peso hits new low as unrest goes on\par     * Weak China, Germany data spark growth concerns\par     * Mexico peso, Brazil real track global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower\par     * Brazil, Chile, Colombia stocks gain\par \par     By Sagarika Jaisinghani and Susan Mathew\par     Nov 14 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso slipped ahead of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting on Thursday where policymakers are widely expected\par to cut rates while the Chilean peso hit a new low as widespread\par anti-government protests showed no signs of abating.\par     An index of Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par for the ninth straight session as a sharp slowdown in China's\par factory output in October and persistent weakness in Germany's\par economy sparked fears of sluggish global growth.\par     The Mexican peso shed 0.5% in the run up to the\par meeting of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2 , known as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Analysts expect\par it to cut the country's benchmark lending rate for the third\par time this year.\par     But a broad rise in longer-dated bond yields over the past\par month suggests Mexico's economic outlook has improved\par relatively, easing "pressure on policy makers to cut more than\par 25 bp today," Morgan Stanley analyst James Lord wrote in a note.\par     "The recent events in the Andean region that have negatively\par impacted broader LatAm sentiment could also be a factor\par prompting a more cautious approach from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2 ."\par     The Chilean peso hit an all-time low of 807.60 to the\par dollar despite measures announced by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost\par liquidity in the financial system after weeks of often violent\par social unrest. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is on course for six straight sessions of\par declines, its longest losing streak since Aug 5. But Chile's\par dollar-denominated bonds strengthened after the report.\par \par     "This program (by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) is better than\par surprise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and is\par likely to soothe, to an extent, concerns regarding further peso\par depreciation," Credit Suisse analyst Alonso Cervera said.\par     In Brazil, the real extended losses for the third\par session in a row, shrugging off data showing an acceleration in\par economic activity in September and tracking global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par lower as weak indicators from major economies reflected the\par fallout from the Sino-U.S. trade war.\par     Investors have been rattled this month as few details have\par emerged about a potential truce. China said on Thursday it was\par holding "in-depth" talks with Washington and cancelling tariffs\par was an important condition for a deal.\par     The Colombian peso sank to a one-month low ahead of\par third-quarter GDP figures due later in the day.\par     A rise in stocks in Brazil, Chile,\par Argentina and Colombia helped boost the wider\par index tracking Latin American shares by 0.3%.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1449 GMT:\par    \par         Stock indexes                Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                1042.27            -0.15\par  MSCI LatAm                           2661.06             0.27\par  Brazil Bovespa                     106540.10             0.45\par  Mexico IPC                                 -                -\par  Chile SPIPSA                         4484.18             1.63\par                                                \par  Argentina MerVal                    32700.40            1.112\par  Colombia IGBC                       13272.70             0.22\par                                                               \par            \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                           4.1843            -0.35\par  Mexico peso                          19.4448            -0.49\par  Chile peso                             804.8            -1.01\par  Colombia peso                        3448.93            -0.70\par  Peru sol                              3.3908            -0.08\par  Argentina peso (interbank)           59.7100             0.03\par                                                \par  \par  (Reporting by Sagarika Jaisinghani and Susan Mathew in\par Bengaluru; Editing by David Clarke)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-11-14T16:27:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191114efbe03gb1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
