\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Chile's peso touches its worst level in history by political crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Chile's weight hit its worst level against the dollar, due to the political instability that lives, amid an avalanche of protests and accusations of human rights attacks by the government of \uc2 Sebasti\u225\'00\'E1n Pi\u241\'00\'F1era\uc2 . Markets evaluate the announcement of a new Constitution, which has moved to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crossing hit a maximum of 800.15 units per dollar, with a depreciation of up to -5.3%, in the fourth week of protests in the country. The complex situation has unleashed a huge wave of volatility. At its best level yesterday, the Chilean peso played a minimum of 759.05, which means a difference of 41.10 units (5.41 percent).\par \par \uc2 USDCLP Chart by TradingViewChile's finance minister Ignacio Briones told the population that the strong exchange rate rollback "is a sign of concern that we are following very carefully."\u160\'00\'A0"The fall in weight has impacts on prices, inflation, on the entire portfolio of goods we consume and is a concern," the official added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 interveneThe\b0 \highlight\uc2  president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mario Marcel, assured that the monetary institution will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce the decline of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  artificially. The central banker said that the fundamental figures of Chile's economy are strong and that the falls were to be expected after the long period of protests.\par \par \uc2 "Chile has a solvent financial system, low exchange rate exposure of economic operators, a strong fiscal position, an adequate level of international reserves and sovereign wealth funds, inflation expectations anchored at 3 percent," Marcel said a statement issued by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ProtestsThe protests in Chile serve four weeks since their inception. They erupted following the decision of the Government of Pi\u241\'00\'F1era to raise the cost of the Chilean Metro ticket, on the recommendation of a panel of public transport experts. With the move, the cost of the ticket was 830 Chilean pesos, more than one U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Social anger turned to other areas and aroused ancient nonconformities among the population. The situation became more complicated when in the protests, Chileans began to burn down Facilities in the Metro and other public facilities. The government decreed a state of emergency and deployed to military personnel.\par \par \uc2 [email protected]\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191112efbc005i6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
