\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar climbing ignites debate over whether  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  should  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The violent rise of the dollar today, the biggest since being recorded in an exchange rate free float scheme and leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to surpass the $800 mark during the session, ignited the debate among economists as to whether it is time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to oversee market to slow the progress and how it should.\par \par \uc2 Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was eliminated in September 1999, there has been a flexible exchange rate system in Chile where the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is determined by the interaction of market players. However, he has left himself the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when he believes that exchange rate movements are not in line with the long-term fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market was in 2011, when it had to go out and buy dollars at a time when it was trading at $465.\par \par \uc2 The situation, now, went to the other end: a hike that reached $40 intraday shortly before noon.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has influenced the price of the dollar through statements - known as "verbal invention" -, paper tenders or purchases or direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales.\par \par \uc2 Should he \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not now?\par \par \uc2 "Exchange rate reaches $800, levels unimaginable a few weeks ago. Inaction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only ends up feeding perception of risk and short-term macroeconomic deterioration," Jorge Selaive, chief economist at Scotiabank, said in a tweet and who earlier exceeded $780 had indicated that a "containment action of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems necessary very soon."\par \par \uc2 Nathan Pincheira, Fynsa's chief economist, said: "An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales seems unlikely to me at the moment. Short-term dollar swap tenders seem highly likely to do so, to maintain dollar liquidity in the face of significant rate increases in that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few days. Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be in conversation now."\par \par \uc2 C\u233\'00\'E9sar Valencia, alpari economist, argued that $800 levels would be justified, "but the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to do with the real exchange rate. That figure has not been updated."\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Climbing entry ignites debate over whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was first published in La Tercera.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191112efbc0049p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
