\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Most Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  fall on U.S.-China trade uncertainty\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2019\par 21:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices, changes comment)\par     * Brazilian real bucks trend after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso near 3-yr lows \par     * Mexican stocks lead Latam equities higher \par \par     By Agamoni Ghosh\par     Aug 27 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell against\par the U.S. dollar on Tuesday as investors remained on edge over\par twists and turns in the U.S.-China trade dispute, but an index\par of the region's stocks snapped a three-day run of losses.\par     MSCI's index of Latin American stocks rose\par 0.7% but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped 0.3% as investors\par assessed conflicting comments from U.S. and Chinese officials\par over the drawn-out trade dispute.\par     President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  sought to ease tensions by predicting\par another round of talks with Beijing on Monday, although \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's\par foreign ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it had not received any recent phone call\par from the United States on trade.\par     Chile's peso hovered at three-year lows as the price\par of copper, the country's top export, remained near\par two-year lows on worries about damage to industrial activity and\par demand from the prolonged trade dispute.\par    "As a small open economy, with an export basket heavily\par skewed towards copper, the CLP has weakened in recent months,\par following a trajectory that closely matches copper price\par trends," said Gustavo Rangel, chief economist, Latam, at ING.  \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near-term outlook remains closely tied to\par trade war concerns and global growth dynamics."     \par     Chile's Finance Minister announced on Monday $600 million in\par additional stimulus in an effort to kick-start the top copper\par producer's sputtering economy.\par     The Argentine peso shed 1.6% despite an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .      \par     Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday sold $302 million of its\par dollar reserves, breaking a guideline on reserve sales agreed as\par part of its $57 billion standby agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International\par Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sold more than $1 billion of its own\par reserves to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against political uncertainty\par touched off by the left-wing opposition's resounding victory in\par a primary vote this month for October's presidency election.\par     Brazil's real, which has lost nearly 8% this month,\par was the only regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to gain against the dollar after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , offering to sell dollars on the\par spot market.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  president \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roberto Campos Neto\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the economy\par was stable or expanded only slightly in the second quarter,\par indicating that low inflation meant there is room for more\par stimulus.\par     Most stock indices in the region rose with Mexican stocks\par  leading the way, up 1.5%. Stocks in Buenos Aires\par lagged the broader equities trend, ending 4% lower, pressured\par heavily by financials.   \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1915 GMT\par      \par  Stock indexes                                 daily % change\par                           Latest            \par  MSCI Emerging Markets              964.28               0.36\par                                             \par  MSCI LatAm                        2495.83                0.8\par                                             \par  Brazil Bovespa                   97418.26               1.03\par                                             \par  Mexico IPC                       40689.92               1.52\par                                             \par  Chile IPSA                        4645.54               0.63\par                                             \par  Argentina MerVal                 24802.01                 -4\par                                             \par  Colombia IGBC                    12339.44               0.13\par                                             \par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                     daily % change\par                                     Latest  \par  Brazil real                        4.1450              -0.15\par                                             \par  Mexico peso                       20.0086              -0.38\par                                             \par  Chile peso                            722              -0.37\par                                             \par  Colombia peso                     3469.23              -1.10\par  Peru sol                            3.393              -0.32\par                  