\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Chile central bank \highlight\uc2  says not close to  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comment on labor market, background)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the bank's chief said on Thursday, even though Chile's peso has depreciated more than 14 percent versus the U.S. dollar this year, among the steepest declines in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "We have a floating exchange rate policy and as such it isn't part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's normal policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and the truth is that we're not even close to thinking about doing it," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rodrigo Vergara said.\par \par \uc2 Among the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chile's peso has posted the seventh biggest drop versus the greenback in 2014, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the peso's recent depreciation is a way to adjust to the new international scenario Chile's economy faces," Vergara told journalists.\par \par \uc2 The economy of the world's top copper producer has been slowing for several quarters, hampered initially by stagnating investment, most notably in the mining sector, with the slowdown compounded by falling consumption.\par \par \uc2 Growth in 2014 will likely be 1.7 percent, a five-year low, the bank forecast recently. That compares with growth of 4.1 percent in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Despite cooling economy, the labor market has remained in better shape than many had feared. The jobless rate for the August to October period fell to 6.4 percent from 6.6 percent in September to July.\par \par \uc2 But Vergara cautioned the labor market could still feel the effects of the slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lag between what happens with economic activity and what happens in the labor market ... and so we may see an additional deterioration in the labor market in the coming months due to the lower growth in the economy." (Reporting by Felipe Iturrieta; Editing by Peter Galloway; Writing by Anthony Esposito; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-18T16:47:20.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141218eaci00g6j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
