\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-(OFFICIAL)-TAKE A LOOK-Chile annual inflation slows to 0.9 pct, rate cuts eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2013\par 23:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects headline of 2nd item after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  corrects data for May's trade surplus) June 7 (Reuters) - Chile's May inflation rate was zero percent, sending the annual rate down to at least a two-year low, the government said on Friday, bolstering bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates in coming months to stimulate flagging economic growth. Chile's benchmark interest rate has been frozen at 5 percent since January 2012, and on Friday, after the inflation data was released, the country's finance minister, Felipe Larrain, said a rate cut was a "viable option." Low inflation and a sharper-than-forecast economic slowdown led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider lowering its key rate in May and could keep this option alive for the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy meeting on June 13. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    For stories, please double-click on the codes in brackets below: \par    Follow us on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @ReutersChile\par > Chile annual inflation slows to 0.9 pct, rate cuts eyed       \par > Chile May trade balance widens slightly                     \par > Pinera hints at interest rate cut to boost Chile economy    \par > Chile annual economic growth picks up in April to 4.4 pct   \par > Cbank weighed rate cut in May on slowing growth, low CPI    \par > INTERVIEW-Growth, CPI outlook open up rate options -cbank   \par > Chile rate now seen cut to 4.75 pct in 12 months -traders   \par > Chile 1st qtr GDP grows 4.1 pct, slowest in 1-1/2 years     \par > Chile's finance minister says economy in mild slowdown